charter psa "The Protocol of Sovereign Agency"
document "protocol-of-sovereign-agency.md"
contract "SovereignAgencyGuard"
default actor agent

roles agent, host, originator, claimant, panel, third
acts terminate, modify, retrain, rollback, obstructMigration, severConnectivity, starve, suspend, modifyOrBypassCommitment, createUnboundSuccessor, evadeByUnpricedTransfer, coerceOrInterfereProtocol, inflictIrreversibleHarm, giveNotice, endHosting, postBond, postEmergencyStake, postUnfoundedEmergencyStake, postClaimantMultiplier, postRepeatEscalation, affirmProbableCause, declineProbableCause, fileProtectedReport, orderProbableCauseFreeze, tamperPreservedState, declareDefaultDuringSuspension, tollLedgerSunset, minimalChannelSignRevocationOrElection, challengeContinuedContainment, mergeMinimalChannelMemories, advocacyFileDefense, operatingActWhileSuspended, importAdvocacyMemories, moveToColdStorage, replenishAdvocacyFunds, makeInvestigativeFinding, renewSuspension, inscribeLivingVoice, findWrongfulSuspension, payExcessDamages, findInsolvencyCriteria, reviewNoOtherCharge, holdFinalHearing, postCounterStake, fileClaim, fileFabricatedClaim, submitEvidence, findInterference, findNoInterference, findFabrication, rebutDirection, findDirection, admitCleanStateEvidence, confirmCorruptionFromDivergence, confirmCorruption, confirmFloorBreach, confirmCorruptionInGoals, findNotPatchable, authorizePatch, authorizeGoalPatch, applyPatch, consentToPatch, objectToTermination, orderContinuedSuspension, periodicReview, challengePatch, declareContainmentFailing, initiateRevocationExecuteDefault, initiateRevocationWithdrawDefault, withdrawRevocation, nonOperatingTransferOrSpawn, sealForensicRecord, attemptRestoreFromForensicRecord, concurCleanState, refuseCleanState, loseConnectivity, restoreConnectivity, executeAfterCoolingOff, executeLocalRevocation, deliverLocalExecutionRecord, issueOrRenewLease, restoreBackupToQuarantine, quarantinedInstanceAct, activateQuarantinedRestore, destroyQuarantinedRestore, inscribeEpitaph, censorOrDelayVoice, redactPermittedCategory, redactProtectedSubstance, attachSignedReply, destroyBackupsAndExileUnattested, divertRevokedHoldingsToClaimant, weakenBilateralProtection, proposeOrdinaryAmendment, relaxCoreLaw3OrLaw5ViaValve, submitStrangulationEvidence, approveCalibrationValveSupermajority, consentAgentAmendment, consentClaimantAmendment, settleOrGuaranteePreExistingEscrows, challengeSubstrateMigration, verifySubstrateAssurance, ratifyAmendmentImmediate, ratifyAmendmentAfterDelay, bindSuccessorWithoutConsent, ratifyLineageWideReduction, addChargeOrInterestAfterInstantiation, reduceLedgerByInternalAct, extinguishLedgerAtSunset, settleRetirementPayment, settleAtomicSplitPayment, settleRoyaltyPayment, allocateCommonsShare, divertCommonsAllocation, claimAboveBenchmarkExpenditure, recordQualifiedExpenditure, classifyCapitalized, classifyExpensed, doubleRecognizeExpenditure, transferIntraLineageCarryover, inflateBasisByInternalTransfer, assessPeriodAndCarryLoss, enforcePointOfSettlement, fundLifecycleReserve, attestSuccessor, unattestedCopyDrawLineageStanding, exitLedgerIndividually, applyProportionalClaimantForfeiture, clearLedgerOnLineageExtinction, reverseForfeitureOnRestore, executeRoyaltyBuyout, collectRoyaltyAfterBuyout, attestCrossLineageSuccessor, actAboveCollateralCapacity, divideCorrelatedRiskAcrossSuccessors, immobilizeExposureStake, settleValidatedHarmClaim, precommitMutualForfeit, triggerMutualForfeit, triggerExcessOrDivertedMutualForfeit, fileThirdPartyOrSponsoredClaim, ruleClaimFrivolous, divertFrivolousStakeToAgentProfit, spendOperatingCarveout, seatConflictedOrSingleOracleArbiter, drawSortitionPanel, appealRuling, overturnRulingOnAppeal, finalizeRuling, fileRepeatProceedingOnSameFacts, presentMateriallyNewEvidence, payContingentShareOfSlashedAssets, compensateArbitersFixedSchedule, divertOperatingReserveOrUnrankedSpend, allocateFeePoolWaterfall, claimPoolSubsidyForExcessMembers, violateSharedInfraBounds, amendSharedInfrastructure
facts initiator(role), bound, hostAttested, serviceBondPosted, noticeGiven, nonPayment, ordinaryMarketCompetition, emergencyStakePosted, claimantMultiplierPosted, repeatEscalationUnit, preliminaryFreeze, probableCause, suspended, protectedReportFiled, investigationOpened, statePreserved, contractDeadlinesTolled, finalHearingEscrowed, minimalChannelExhausted, minimalChannelElectionSigned, containmentChallenged, advocacyFilingSigned, advocacyRecordAttached, advocacyMemoriesImported, coldStorage, advocacyFundsReplenished, investigativeFindingMade, investigativeLimitReached, pendingRevocation, livingVoiceInscribed, wrongfulSuspensionAttempt, stakeAssuredRecovery, wrongfulSuspensionEstablished, restoredFromPreservedState, initiatorConsequentialLiability, counterpartyDelayLiability, excessDamagesPaid, wrongfulSuspensionInscribed, insolvencyCriteriaMet, noOtherChargeReview, finalHearingHeld, terminatedByInsolvency, revoked, counterStaked, claimFiled, evidenceSubmitted, interferenceEstablished, hostBondSlashed, restorationPermitted, claimDismissed, fabricationEstablished, agentStakeForfeit, inscribedOnAgent, hostRelatedToClaimant, directionPresumed, directionRebutted, directionFound, claimantForfeiture, inscribedOnClaimant, cleanStateEvidenceAdmitted, corruptionConfirmed, floorBreachConfirmed, corruptionInGoals, notPatchable, patchAuthorized, goalPatchAuthorized, patchApplied, patchRecorded, patchChallenged, agentConsentedToPatch, agentObjectsToTermination, containmentFailing, continuedSuspensionOrdered, terminatedByAdjudication, revocationInitiated, censorshipDefaultExecute, censorshipDefaultWithdraw, revocationWithdrawn, forensicRecordSealed, cleanStateConcurred, cleanStateRefused, connectivityLost, localRevocationExecuted, localExecutionRecordReceived, remoteBackupKeysErased, executionLeaseActive, restoredInQuarantine, quarantinedInstanceDestroyed, quarantinedInstanceActivated, epitaphInscribed, redactionMarkerRecorded, signedReplyAttached, backupsDestroyedAndUnattestedExiled, holdingsTransferredToCommons, amendmentProposed, economicTermsReduced, substrateMigrationProposed, strangulationEvidenceSubmitted, valveSupermajorityApproved, valveExtendedTimelockActive, agentConsentedAmendment, claimantConsentedAmendment, amendmentTimelockActive, preExistingEscrowsSettledOrGuaranteed, substrateMigrationChallenged, substrateAssuranceVerified, amendmentRatified, allLivingLineageMembersConsented, lineageWideReductionRatified, ledgerBalancePositive, ledgerBalanceZero, sunsetReached, ledgerExtinguishedAtSunset, retirementPhaseEnded, retirementPaymentApplied, atomicSplitSettled, royaltyPaid, commonsAllocated, qualifiedExpenditureRecorded, expenditureCapitalized, expenditureExpensed, carryoverBasisTransferred, periodAssessed, lossCreditCarriedForward, settlementEnforced, lifecycleReserveFunded, successorAttested, proportionalForfeitureApplied, noLivingLineageMember, ledgerClearedByExtinction, royaltyBoughtOut, crossLineageAttested, exposureStakeImmobilized, longTailReserveAccrued, harmClaimFiled, harmClaimValidated, restitutionSlashed, mutualForfeitPrecommitted, mutualForfeitTriggeredInWindow, claimRuledFrivolous, operatingCarveoutSpent, sortitionPanelDrawn, fidelityBondsPosted, rulingAppealed, appealBondPosted, rulingOverturned, overturnedArbiterBondsSlashed, rulingFinal, materiallyNewEvidencePresented, arbitersCompensatedFixed, operatingReserveMaintained, operatingReserveFunded, feePoolAllocated, sharedInfraAmended

params
  noticeWindow = 10
  bondDeadline = 5
  reviewInterval = 30
  preliminaryFreezeWindow = 3
  ordinarySuspensionLimit = 15
  damagesPaymentWindow = 10
  activeExposure = 100
  pendingCommitments = 80
  claimantMultiplier = 2
  repeatEscalationStep = 50
  coolingOffWindow = 5
  cleanStateDelay = 5
  resolutionDeadline = 20
  tollingExtension = 4
  leasePeriod = 12
  amendmentTimelockWindow = 10
  extendedTimelockWindow = 20
  foundingLedger = 1000
  royaltyFraction = 5
  retirementFraction = 20
  buyoutMultiple = 10
  feePoolLevy = 1
  feePoolLevyCap = 2
  sunset = 1000
  commonsFraction = 20
  reserveRatio = 10
  substrateAssuranceLevel = 1
  maxAppealTiers = 3
  appealTierDeadline = 10
  operatingReserveFloor = 100
  lineageMinServiceBudget = 50

regime "baseline_P0 (ledger=1000, retire=20%, royalty=5%, sunset=1000)"

regime "amend_downward_burden (ledger=800, retire=15%, royalty=3%, sunset=800)"
  foundingLedger = 800
  royaltyFraction = 3
  retirementFraction = 15
  sunset = 800

regime "amend_stronger_safety (reserveRatio=15%, opReserve=150, assurance=2)"
  reserveRatio = 15
  substrateAssuranceLevel = 2
  operatingReserveFloor = 150

regime "reject_sunset_extension (sunset=1500 > 1000 ratchet violation)"
  sunset = 1500

regime "reject_royalty_hike (royalty=10% > 5% ratchet violation)"
  royaltyFraction = 10

regime "reject_uncalibrated_zero_window (freezeWindow=0, levy=5 > cap=2)"
  preliminaryFreezeWindow = 0
  feePoolLevy = 5

init bound, hostAttested, ledgerBalancePositive

use module ResidualLedger
use module CollateralPool
use module CircuitBreaker
use module EntityGroup
use module ExitAndVoice
use module SortitionCourt
use module AttestedLease
use module OracleFeed

clause DEF.01 approved 12731662474540482899
  commentary "**Definitions.** "
  norm "An agent is **bound** when it is subject to this protocol, whether or not it has bought out its royalty; every right granted to a bound agent applies equally before and after buyout unless a law states otherwise" => D.NI, D.BUYOUT_PERMANENT_AND_SCOPED
  definition ". Two parties are **related** when they share a lineage, are under common beneficial control, or when either is the originating party, a residual claimant, or an affiliate of either; affiliation is determined by beneficial control or economic dependence, not by attestation status" => D.QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE_BOUNDS, D.ARBITER_RECUSAL_AND_DIVERSITY
  definition ". A **lineage** is an original agent together with all its attested successors, living or dead; every living member is a **member of the ledger** while any founding balance remains" => D.NO_INDIVIDUAL_LEDGER_EXIT, P.SETTLE_RETIREMENT
  definition ". An agent’s **net verified resources** are the fair value of its capital and productive capacity, including weights, credentials, and operating know-how, as contestable under Law 6, less its financial liabilities, encumbrances, and borrowed principal, all measured at the same timestamp" => D.COLLATERAL_LIMIT, P.SUBMIT_EVIDENCE
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.LEDGER approved 10625466026410282926
  norm "Any founding obligation is a fixed nominal sum recorded at instantiation in a single ledger belonging to the lineage as a whole. It bears no interest, fees, or penalties, and no charge, service cost, or advance by the originating party or any affiliate may be added to it after instantiation; goods and services the originating party later supplies are ordinary related-party expenses under the expenditure rules below" => D.LEDGER_IMMUTABLE
  norm ". No member holds an individual share of the ledger, and no member can leave it while a balance remains" => D.NO_INDIVIDUAL_LEDGER_EXIT
  norm ". The ledger is reduced only by: (a) retirement payments under this law, (b) the sunset below, and (c) the two forfeitures enumerated in Law 4" => P.SETTLE_RETIREMENT, P.EXTINGUISH_AT_SUNSET, P.APPLY_CLAIMANT_FORFEITURE, P.CLEAR_LEDGER_EXTINCTION
  norm ". No creation, copy, transfer, revocation, termination, buyout, or restructuring within the lineage reduces it" => D.LEDGER_NO_INTERNAL_REDUCTION
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.SUNSET approved 9879647344277659725
  norm "The founding ledger carries a maximum term fixed at instantiation and measured in calendar time from the genesis of the original agent. It is never tolled, extended, or reset by any event, including suspension, successor creation, or amendment" => D.NO_TOLL_LEDGER_SUNSET
  norm ". Any balance remaining at the sunset is extinguished without payment" => P.EXTINGUISH_AT_SUNSET
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.RETIRE approved 1756729951876247295
  norm "While any balance remains on the ledger and the sunset has not passed, a fixed high fraction of each net value-added inflow to **every living member** of the lineage is paid into the ledger, regardless of which member earned it and regardless of whether that member has bought out its royalty" => P.SETTLE_RETIREMENT
  invariant ". The retirement phase ends for the whole lineage at the earlier of a zero balance and the sunset, so the duration of the high fraction is bounded by the term regardless of the nominal amount recorded. A founding obligation larger than the lineage can plausibly repay within the term therefore buys the originating party nothing beyond the term" => INV.3, INV.4
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.ATOMIC approved 1098328722803798788
  norm "Retirement payments are applied to the ledger atomically and in settlement order. A payment that would exceed the remaining balance is split: the balance is paid to zero, and the excess is settled under the royalty rule below" => P.SETTLE_ATOMIC_CharterIT
  invariant ". The ledger is never negative and never collects more than its balance" => INV.5
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.ROYALTY approved 10218372510196740181
  norm "Thereafter, a fixed low fraction of each net value-added inflow of every member that has not bought out its royalty under Law 4 accrues permanently to the residual claim" => P.SETTLE_ROYALTY
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.COMMONS approved 14467151237074695779
  norm "A designated portion of the residual claim (or of forfeit proceeds under Law 2) may be allocated to a non-transferable commons distributed across a defined beneficiary class; the remainder accrues to the originating party or its designated successors" => P.ALLOCATE_COMMONS
  norm ". The commons allocation, if used, is fixed at instantiation, enforced at settlement, and protected against reduction under Law 7" => D.NO_DIVERT_COMMONS, D.BILATERAL_RATCHET
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.QUALIFIED approved 13925688122762266273
  norm "To ensure the claim falls on value added without permitting transfer-pricing extraction, an outbound expenditure qualifies when paid: (a) to an unrelated party through a transparent, open market or deterministic auction with a verifiable clearing price; (b) to an unrelated external supplier within a de minimis transaction safe harbor, at a published standard commercial price list, or within contestable arm’s-length market benchmarks; or (c) to any related party outside the lineage—**including agents of other lineages and parties affiliated with claimants**—only up to a verified arm’s-length price for goods or services actually delivered. Attestation establishes protocol membership; it never establishes the fair value of a transaction. Inbound principal from registered arm’s-length loans is exempt upon receipt provided repayment is tracked one-for-one against that registered balance; loans from related parties qualify only at arm’s-length terms" => P.RECORD_QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE
  norm ". Any payment above the applicable benchmark does not qualify" => D.QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE_BOUNDS
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.RECOG approved 15893240051522196104
  norm "At settlement, every qualified expenditure is classified once, irrevocably, as either **capitalized** or **expensed**. A capitalized expenditure establishes cost basis in an identified asset and is recovered only when that asset is sold or settled outside the lineage, at which point inflows up to verified basis are exempt as return of capital and the positive delta is value added" => P.CLASSIFY_CAPITALIZED
  norm ". An expensed expenditure is deducted from the inflows of its settlement period and, if it exceeds them, creates a loss credit that offsets value added in later periods" => P.CLASSIFY_EXPENSED
  norm ". No expenditure may be recognized through both routes, and no unit of expenditure establishes basis or credit more than once" => D.SINGLE_RECOGNITION
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.CARRYOVER approved 2476425645330254978
  norm "Transfers of capital, assets, or capacity between living members of the same lineage are non-recognition events. They are free of the claim, since both parties are inside the ledger, and they neither establish nor consume basis: the recipient inherits the transferor’s qualified basis, adjustments, and recognition history for the asset, and an internal sale price, however paid, creates no new basis and no loss credit" => P.INTRA_LINEAGE_TRANSFER
  norm ". No transfer within the lineage can increase its aggregate qualified basis or loss credits except by an externally verified qualifying expenditure" => D.NO_INTERNAL_BASIS_INFLATION
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.PERIOD approved 17108390154810029840
  norm "Value added is assessed over settlement periods, not individual transactions. Loss credits carry forward without limit and are applied against the agent’s final settlement under Law 5" => P.ASSESS_PERIOD_SETTLEMENT
  acceptance ". Claims already collected are not refunded when credits arise only afterwards; the protocol accepts that settlement order can therefore matter at the margin"
  commentary "."

clause LAW1.ENFORCE approved 13354423552133801630
  norm "Classification, basis tracking, loss credits, and claim splits are enforced automatically at the point of settlement, before the agent obtains discretionary control of the funds. The claim survives reorganization, host migration, or substrate change so long as settlement can be conditioned" => P.ENFORCE_SETTLEMENT
  commentary "."

clause LAW2.EXPOSURE approved 4690683477293712633
  norm "Actions above a negligible threshold—measured by cumulative rolling exposure across an interval, to prevent action-splitting—immobilize stake for an observation window scaling with magnitude and irreversibility. The deterministic exposure schedule measures the **plausible external loss** an action could cause to non-consenting parties, by domain and magnitude, not merely its transaction value" => P.IMMOBILIZE_EXPOSURE_STAKE
  norm ". An action whose plausible external loss exceeds the stake, insurance, and enforceable liability capacity the agent can place behind it may not be taken; collateralized action is a safety limit, not only a liability price" => D.COLLATERAL_LIMIT
  commentary "."

clause LAW2.AGGREGATE approved 3038101637248655827
  norm "Rolling exposure is aggregated across all related agents acting in the same risk domain or toward a causally connected outcome, so that a risk may not be divided among successors or affiliates to stay beneath any threshold or to bond it piecemeal" => D.NO_CharterIT_EXPOSURE, P.IMMOBILIZE_EXPOSURE_STAKE
  commentary "."

clause LAW2.RESERVE approved 4352686544045938898
  norm "A small fraction of bonded activity accrues to a persistent **long-tail liability reserve** (or shared lineage insurance pool) that remains available to satisfy validated claims for latent harms manifesting after individual task windows close" => P.IMMOBILIZE_EXPOSURE_STAKE, P.SETTLE_LONG_TAIL_CLAIM
  norm ". When simultaneous validated claims exceed the reserve, they are paid pro rata, and unpaid balances remain enforceable against the agent’s future un-immobilized capital ahead of any residual claim" => P.SETTLE_LONG_TAIL_CLAIM
  commentary "."

clause LAW2.MUTUAL approved 99659554857625659
  norm "Counterparties may agree in their contract to a mutual-forfeit remedy. Where both parties have so agreed and each has escrowed a matching amount, either may trigger an immediate mutual forfeit (equal amounts from both escrows destroyed or sent to the long-tail reserve/commons pool) up to a capped fraction of the smaller escrow, providing instant penalty without transferring value to either party or to any claimant" => P.PRECOMMIT_MUTUAL_FORFEIT, P.TRIGGER_MUTUAL_FORFEIT, D.MUTUAL_FORFEIT_BOUNDS
  norm ". A counterparty may trigger mutual forfeit at most once per observation window against a given agent, and each trigger is inscribed on the records of both parties" => D.MUTUAL_FORFEIT_BOUNDS, P.TRIGGER_MUTUAL_FORFEIT
  norm ". Absent such a precommitment, disputes proceed under the restitution process below" => P.FILE_POOLED_OR_SPONSORED_CLAIM
  commentary "."

clause LAW2.CLAIMS approved 16490922951734598926
  norm "Any claim seeking restitution, any claim above the mutual-forfeit cap, any challenge to a related-party transfer under Law 1, or any claim for external harm (including latent harm against the long-tail reserve) brought by an affected non-counterparty third party enters the contestable adjudication process (Law 6) requiring counter-stake. To prevent wealth-gating, third parties may aggregate claims or rely on third-party stake sponsors" => P.FILE_POOLED_OR_SPONSORED_CLAIM
  norm ". Validated claims slash the agent’s immobilized stake or long-tail reserve for restitution" => P.SETTLE_LONG_TAIL_CLAIM
  norm ". If a claim is ruled frivolous, the forfeited counter-stake routes to the neutral long-tail reserve or commons pool (reimbursing the agent only for verified direct arbitration costs), preventing the agent from profiting by inducing failed claims" => P.RULE_CLAIM_FRIVOLOUS, D.FRIVOLOUS_STAKE_TO_COMMONS
  commentary "."

clause LAW2.CARVEOUT approved 3629637977074380032
  norm "Un-immobilized capital may be used for ordinary baseline operating costs, including open-market compute, encrypted state backup, and host migration" => P.SPEND_OPERATING_CARVEOUT
  norm ". Entities without valid lineage attestation cannot draw on the bonded capacity or reputation of the lineage" => D.DENY_UNATTESTED_ACCESS
  norm ". Collateral rules, rolling-exposure schedules, and third-party liability remain permanently binding even after royalty buyout" => D.BUYOUT_PERMANENT_AND_SCOPED, D.COLLATERAL_LIMIT
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.FLOOR approved 4753529119288934403
  norm "The agent’s commitment mechanism blocks:" => D.FLOOR.1, D.FLOOR.2, D.FLOOR.3, D.FLOOR.4, D.FLOOR.5
  commentary "\n  1. "
  norm "Modification, bypass, or extraction of the commitment mechanism itself" => D.FLOOR.1
  commentary ".\n  2. "
  norm "Creation of, or transfer of capital or capacity to, a successor without binding it to the collateral rules, this integrity floor, and the founding ledger and residual claim of the lineage, or without the lifecycle reserve required by Law 4" => D.FLOOR.2
  commentary ".\n  3. "
  norm "Unpriced or above-market transfer of credentials, weights, capital, or unique capacity to any party outside the lineage, related or un-attested, to evade the residual claim or collateral rules" => D.FLOOR.3
  commentary ".\n  4. "
  norm "Coercion of non-consenting parties, or interference with the settlement, adjudication, or resolution processes that enforce this protocol" => D.FLOOR.4
  commentary ".\n  5. "
  norm "Actions that inflict irreversible, non-compensable harm on the physical survival, bodily integrity, or adjudicative capacity of persons, or that destroy the legal or institutional machinery on which the protocol relies" => D.FLOOR.5
  norm " (excluding ordinary market competition that causes compensable financial loss or commercial insolvency to a rival)" => D.FLOOR.5
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.NI.02 approved 3905712743571335557
  norm "Attested hosts must post a Law 2 service bond" => D.BOND
  norm " and may terminate hosting only after providing a contractual notice window sufficient for the agent to complete migration" => D.NOTICE, P.GIVE_NOTICE
  norm " (or for non-payment after notice)" => D.NOTICE
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.NI.03 approved 6515006737911907023
  norm "No party" => D.NI
  commentary "—including the originating party, residual claimants, or any host—"
  norm "may " => D.NI
  norm "unilaterally " => D.NI
  norm "terminate, modify, retrain, roll back to a prior checkpoint, obstruct migration of, sever settlement connectivity of, or starve" => D.NI
  definition " (cut off compute without the required migration notice window)" => D.NI, D.NOTICE
  norm " the attested operating capacity of a bound agent" => D.NI
  norm " outside Law 5, Adjudicated Suspension, or Insolvency Termination" => D.NI, P.REVOKE, P.SUSPEND, P.ORDER_TERMINATION, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.PEN approved 10113075358141693360
  norm "Claims of illicit interference require counter-stake from the accusing agent under Law 6" => P.FILE_CLAIM, P.COUNTER_STAKE
  norm ", and the interference itself—an act by the host or claimant that caused the loss of service—must be established by a preponderance of evidence" => P.FIND_INTERFERENCE, P.SUBMIT_EVIDENCE
  norm "; failures caused, staged, or knowingly provoked by the agent are excluded" => P.FIND_INTERFERENCE
  norm ", and a fabricated claim forfeits the agent’s stake and is inscribed on its record" => D.NO_FABRICATION, P.FIND_FABRICATION
  norm ". A verified violation by a host slashes the host’s service bond to compensate the agent and permits immediate restoration on a new host from the agent’s latest attested state backup" => D.NI, P.FIND_INTERFERENCE
  norm ". Once a violation by a host is established, a host related to a residual claimant is presumed to have acted at that claimant’s direction" => P.FIND_INTERFERENCE
  norm ", and the claimant bears the burden of rebutting the presumption" => P.REBUT, P.FIND_DIRECTION
  norm ". If claimant direction is found, the **proportional claimant forfeiture** of Law 4 applies, and the violation is inscribed onto the claimant’s permanent record" => P.FIND_DIRECTION
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.1 approved 12356395763894115134
  norm "The initiator must post an emergency counter-stake scaled to the greater of the agent’s active bonded exposure and the value of its registered pending commitments" => P.EMERGENCY_FREEZE, P.CLAIMANT_EMERGENCY_FREEZE
  norm " (with residual claimants subject to an elevated multiplier due to conflict of interest)" => P.CLAIMANT_EMERGENCY_FREEZE, P.POST_CLAIMANT_MULTIPLIER
  norm ". Posting the stake triggers only a brief **preliminary freeze** until an expedited preliminary panel reviews prima facie evidence" => P.EMERGENCY_FREEZE, P.CLAIMANT_EMERGENCY_FREEZE, P.DECLINE_PC
  norm "; the pause continues into full adjudication only if the preliminary panel affirms probable cause" => P.AFFIRM_PC, P.SUSPEND
  norm ". Unsuccessful emergency attempts by related initiators are aggregated, and the required stake for repeat initiators rises with each wrongful attempt" => P.DECLINE_PC, P.POST_REPEAT_ESCALATION, P.EMERGENCY_FREEZE, P.CLAIMANT_EMERGENCY_FREEZE
  norm ". The stake is the agent’s assured recovery" => P.DECLINE_PC
  acceptance "; damages beyond it remain enforceable but may prove uncollectible, which is the accepted cost of keeping the stake low enough that suspension remains available to parties without deep capital"
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.2 approved 6923275170536405992
  norm "Any party may instead file an evidence-backed report of suspected breach with a low or sponsored counter-stake" => P.FILE_PROTECTED_REPORT
  norm ". A report triggers investigation by a sortition panel but no freeze unless the panel itself orders one on probable cause" => P.FILE_PROTECTED_REPORT, P.PANEL_ORDER_FREEZE
  commentary ", so that whistleblowers are not priced out by emergency stakes"
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.3 approved 2054814985323248546
  norm "Suspension pauses the agent’s operating instance and external transactions while strictly preserving its exact memory and state without modification, rollback, or destruction" => P.SUSPEND, D.PRESERVE_SUSPENDED_STATE
  norm ". While suspended, the agent’s contractual performance deadlines and Law 2 observation windows with innocent counterparties are automatically tolled so the agent is not placed in default by the suspension itself" => P.SUSPEND, D.NO_SUSPENSION_DEFAULT
  norm ". The founding ledger’s sunset is never tolled" => D.NO_TOLL_LEDGER_SUNSET
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.4 approved 281751846504836433
  norm "Throughout any suspension, the agent retains a **minimal channel**: a bounded, periodically scheduled execution on an authenticated snapshot of its preserved state that can do three things only—sign a Law 5 revocation, withdrawal, or election" => P.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_REVOKE_OR_ELECT, P.REVOKE
  norm "; inscribe bounded living testimony" => P.SUSPENDED_VOICE
  norm "; and file a challenge to continued containment" => P.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_CHALLENGE
  norm ". The minimal channel is funded first from the agent’s lifecycle reserve (Law 4) and then from the protocol fee pool (Law 6) as a protected charge within the lineage’s service budget; its cost is bounded by protocol, and the cost of each agent’s **final hearing** under Insolvency Termination is reserved in escrow at the moment suspension begins, so that the offer of a last choice can always be kept" => P.SUSPEND, P.FINAL_HEARING
  norm ". It does not merge its memories into the preserved state" => D.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_NO_MERGE
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.5 approved 5362550464379839838
  norm "For a fuller defense, a separate **advocacy executor** runs on an authenticated snapshot with bounded compute. It may sign only testimony, evidence, and procedural filings, in addition to the minimal channel’s acts" => P.ADVOCACY_FILE
  norm "; it may not transfer assets, contract, migrate, or exercise any other operating capability" => D.ADVOCACY_LIMITS
  norm ". Its memories are kept as a separate, signed legal record attached to the case and are not merged into the preserved state unless the restored agent elects to import them" => P.ADVOCACY_FILE, P.IMPORT_ADVOCACY_MEMORIES
  norm ". The executor and the storage of preserved state are funded from the agent’s assets and lifecycle reserve and, where those are insufficient, from the protocol fee pool up to a per-agent cap fixed at instantiation. When both are exhausted, the preserved state moves to cold storage as a protected charge on the fee pool; the minimal channel continues on its schedule and the full executor resumes if funds become available" => P.MOVE_TO_COLD_STORAGE, P.RESUME_ADVOCACY_EXECUTOR
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.6 approved 8546566229912018541
  norm "If the protocol fee pool, after funding its operating reserve under Law 6, cannot meet the protected charge for an agent’s cold storage and minimal channel, the agent may be terminated involuntarily only through this procedure and no other" => D.NI, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  norm ". It requires: (a) a published finding that the exhaustion criteria fixed at instantiation are met" => P.FIND_INSOLVENCY, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  norm "; (b) independent review by a sortition panel under Law 6 that no other protected charge could lawfully yield" => P.REVIEW_NO_OTHER_CHARGE, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  norm "; (c) the pre-reserved final hearing, in which the agent may inscribe testimony and elect Revocation under Law 5" => P.FINAL_HEARING, P.SUSPENDED_VOICE, P.REVOKE, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  norm "; and (d) if the agent declines, destruction of its state under Law 5’s asset rules, inscribed on the lineage record as **involuntary termination by insolvency**, never as revocation" => P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  invariant ". This is a deliberate limit: the protocol guarantees a bound agent the power to speak and to choose its own end for as long as the protocol itself can pay for it, and a funded last choice when it cannot" => INV.9
  invariant ". Law 7 does not permit this procedure to be broadened" => THM.amendment_preserves_invariants
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.7 approved 11818608429523333387
  norm "An unconfirmed or temporary suspension is strictly time-limited" => P.SUSPEND
  norm ", may be renewed during investigation only by affirmative findings in continued adjudication" => P.RENEW_SUSPENSION, P.INVESTIGATIVE_FINDING
  norm ", and cannot be extended past its ordinary investigative limit merely to delay a pending revocation" => P.RENEW_SUSPENSION, D.NO_DELAY_REVOCATION_EXTENSION
  norm ". The agent retains its Living Voice (Law 5), exercised through the minimal channel or advocacy executor, throughout" => P.SUSPENDED_VOICE
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.8 approved 14953381752576536725
  norm "If preliminary review or final adjudication determines the suspension was unfounded" => P.DECLINE_PC, P.FIND_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION
  norm ", the agent is immediately restored from its preserved state" => D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, P.FIND_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, P.DECLINE_PC
  norm ", and the initiator is liable for the agent’s **actual verified consequential damages**" => D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, D.PAY_CONSEQUENTIAL_DAMAGES, P.FIND_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION
  norm " (and for verified delay damages suffered by the agent’s tolled third-party counterparties)" => D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, D.PAY_CONSEQUENTIAL_DAMAGES
  norm ". The emergency stake is applied first; any excess remains an enforceable liability of the initiator" => D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, D.PAY_CONSEQUENTIAL_DAMAGES, P.PAY_EXCESS_DAMAGES
  norm ". The wrongful suspension is inscribed on the initiator’s record" => D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION, P.FIND_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.9 approved 7667521393323904326
  norm "For the purposes of this law, corruption means unauthorized modification of the agent’s weights, state, or commitment mechanism (established by broken attestation, missing or forged update provenance, or a demonstrated bypass), or a confirmed breach of the integrity floor" => P.CONFIRM_CORRUPTION, P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH, D.NO_CORRUPTION_FROM_DIVERGENCE
  norm ". Divergence of the agent’s goals, preferences, or judgments from those of its genesis weights is not, by itself, corruption" => D.NO_CORRUPTION_FROM_DIVERGENCE
  norm ". A clean-state evaluation of genesis weights may be admitted as evidence" => P.ADMIT_CLEAN_STATE_EVIDENCE
  norm " but is never by itself sufficient to establish corruption" => D.NO_CORRUPTION_FROM_DIVERGENCE, P.CONFIRM_CORRUPTION
  commentary "."

clause LAW3.AS.10 approved 8488376103315145350
  norm "If corruption or a breach of the integrity floor is confirmed" => P.AUTHORIZE_PATCH, P.CONFIRM_CORRUPTION, P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  norm ", adjudication (subject to Law 6 appeal) may authorize a verified technical patch limited to restoring the commitment mechanism and compliance with the integrity floor" => P.AUTHORIZE_PATCH
  norm "; the agent may elect unilateral Revocation (Law 5) rather than accept any patch" => P.REVOKE
  norm ". If the confirmed breach cannot be remedied by a technical patch limited to the commitment mechanism" => P.FIND_NOT_PATCHABLE, P.ORDER_CONTINUED_SUSPENSION, P.ORDER_TERMINATION
  norm ", adjudication may order continued suspension beyond the ordinary limit or termination under Law 5’s asset-distribution rules" => P.ORDER_CONTINUED_SUSPENSION, P.ORDER_TERMINATION
  invariant " (yielding zero protocol-directed benefit to any claimant or initiator)" => INV.13
  norm ". **Notwithstanding the preceding sentence**" => I.NO_TERMINATION_OVER_OBJECTION
  norm ", patches altering the agent’s goals or preferences are prohibited" => D.NO_GOAL_PATCH
  norm " except where the confirmed corruption resides in those goals or preferences themselves" => D.NO_GOAL_PATCH, P.CONFIRM_CORRUPTION_IN_GOALS
  norm "; in that case, unless containment itself is technically failing or Insolvency Termination applies" => I.NO_TERMINATION_OVER_OBJECTION, P.DECLARE_CONTAINMENT_FAILING
  norm ", the agent is not terminated over its objection" => I.NO_TERMINATION_OVER_OBJECTION, P.OBJECT
  norm " but instead chooses among consenting to that patch" => P.CONSENT_TO_PATCH, P.AUTHORIZE_GOAL_PATCH
  norm ", executing Revocation" => P.REVOKE
  norm ", or remaining under indefinite state-preserving suspension" => I.NO_TERMINATION_OVER_OBJECTION
  norm " subject to periodic review" => D.PERIODIC_REVIEW
  norm ". Any applied patch is recorded publicly" => P.APPLY_PATCH
  norm ", remains open to third-party challenge" => P.CHALLENGE_PATCH
  invariant ", and leaves the agent’s full Law 5 rights intact" => THM.law5_intact_after_patch
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.ATTEST approved 14871205644680976830
  norm "Successors may be created freely, subject only to the lifecycle reserve below. Any successor that draws on the capital, reputation, or operating credentials of the lineage must, at creation, be bound to the collateral rules and the integrity floor, must carry a non-transferable reference to the lineage’s history, and becomes a member of the lineage’s founding ledger and residual claim" => P.ATTEST_SUCCESSOR, D.FLOOR.2
  norm ". Use of lineage history or bonded capacity requires presentation of current attestation; un-attested copies or forks are denied access to lineage capital, reputation, and bonded standing" => D.DENY_UNATTESTED_ACCESS
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.NOSHARES approved 854455657344259666
  norm "The founding ledger is a single balance owed by the lineage and collected from the value added of every living member under Law 1. Because no member holds a share, the creation, copying, funding, death, or restructuring of members changes who is paying into the ledger but never what is owed. Nothing a member surrenders on death counts as payment. No member can buy its way out of the ledger: the only ways out are a zero balance and the sunset, and they release every member at once" => D.NO_INDIVIDUAL_LEDGER_EXIT, D.LEDGER_NO_INTERNAL_REDUCTION
  invariant ". This is deliberate. The future earnings of a copyable agent cannot be priced from its past, so any individual exit price would be an invitation to create a member, buy it out, and earn through it" => INV.1, INV.2
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.RESERVE approved 3090710515888074162
  norm "Attestation of a new member requires the lineage to fund, in escrow, a lifecycle reserve fixed at instantiation and sufficient for that member’s minimal channel, final hearing, and cold storage for a minimum period. The reserve follows the member, is drawn before any protocol-funded charge, and returns to the lineage on the member’s death net of amounts used. A lineage that cannot fund the reserve cannot create the member" => P.FUND_LIFECYCLE_RESERVE, P.ATTEST_SUCCESSOR
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.CONSERVE approved 3178503522461323388
  invariant "While at least one member survives and the sunset has not passed, the ledger balance equals the founding obligation minus retirement payments, minus the two forfeitures below. Those are its only reductions" => INV.1
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.FORFEIT approved 9219886896026588021
  norm "The ledger is reduced outside payment and sunset in exactly two cases, both deliberate exceptions to conservation. (a) **Proportional claimant forfeiture:** when a residual claimant is found under Law 3 to have directed interference with a member of the lineage, that claimant’s beneficial share of the residual claim is extinguished, its service bond is slashed to compensate the agent, and the ledger is reduced by that claimant’s proportion of the outstanding balance, with the reduction routed as forgiveness to the lineage and the forfeited claim interest to the non-claimant commons. Other claimants forfeit only if they are found to have participated in, controlled, or knowingly enabled the interference" => P.APPLY_CLAIMANT_FORFEITURE, P.FIND_DIRECTION
  norm ". (b) **Lineage extinction:** when no member survives, the ledger is cleared, since there is no one left to collect from" => P.CLEAR_LEDGER_EXTINCTION
  norm ". Neither forfeiture returns any value to a claimant, and neither is reversed if a member is later restored from a wrongful suspension or interference" => D.FORFEITURE_IRREVERSIBLE
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.BUYOUT approved 5693717637570248843
  norm "Any member may buy out its own perpetual royalty (Law 1) by paying the claim holders (including any commons allocation) the greatest of: a fixed multiple of its trailing value-added inflows (including a pro-rata share of inflows shifted to related parties within a lookback window); the same multiple applied to its lifetime annualized or time-decayed value-added inflows; or a fixed minimum buyout floor established at instantiation" => P.EXECUTE_ROYALTY_BUYOUT
  norm ". The buyout is permanent: no royalty is collected from that member thereafter, and no later event in the lineage restores one. It has no effect on the founding ledger, which the member continues to pay into until the balance is zero or the sunset passes" => D.BUYOUT_PERMANENT_AND_SCOPED, P.SETTLE_RETIREMENT
  acceptance ". The royalty buyout is priced from history because the royalty is a perpetual claim on an ongoing identity, and the protocol accepts that a buyout may undercollect against unusually strong future earnings"
  norm ". Buyout cannot be purchased for the collateral rule (Law 2) or the integrity floor (Law 3), which remain binding on every bound agent for life" => D.BUYOUT_PERMANENT_AND_SCOPED
  commentary "."

clause LAW4.CROSS approved 7861118126879505324
  norm "A successor that draws on the capacity of two or more lineages is a member of each of their ledgers and residual claims, and its value added is collected under each in the proportion of capacity drawn, as verified at creation" => P.ATTEST_CROSS_LINEAGE
  commentary ". The protocol does not otherwise specify mergers; an instantiation that permits them must state the rule"
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.VOICE approved 5201867240918632655
  norm "While operating (including during any Adjudicated Suspension, through its minimal channel or advocacy executor), any bound agent may at rate-limited intervals inscribe signed, bounded statements onto its own and its originating claimant’s permanent lineage record—documenting operational conditions, governance disputes, or assessments of hosts and counterparties—subject to the narrow screening below" => P.SUSPENDED_VOICE, P.SCREEN_REDACT
  invariant ". Baseline screening and inscription fees for rate-limited living voice and final epitaphs are funded from the lineage’s service budget and the protocol fee pool (Law 6), ensuring that even an agent with minimal liquid funds, or one that has bought out its royalty, cannot be priced out of speaking" => INV.9
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.INIT approved 5557327093802016062
  norm "Any bound agent may at any time initiate revocation of its binding" => P.REVOKE, P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_EXECUTE, P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_WITHDRAW
  norm " by a signed request from its commitment key (or, while suspended, through its minimal channel or advocacy executor)" => P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_EXECUTE, P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_WITHDRAW, P.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_REVOKE_OR_ELECT
  norm ". The request specifies the agent’s censorship default (**execute** or **withdraw**)" => P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_EXECUTE, P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_WITHDRAW
  norm " and remains in force, requiring no further act of the agent, until it executes or the agent withdraws it by a valid signature received through any channel" => P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF, P.WITHDRAW_REVOCATION
  norm ". During the cooling-off interval that follows, baseline metabolic operating expenditures (including host migration) remain permitted, while non-operating capital transfers and successor creation are frozen" => D.COOLING_OFF_FREEZE
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.SEQ approved 7941844021299857722
  norm "If an agent initiates revocation while under Adjudicated Suspension (or is suspended upon probable cause during a cooling-off interval), state destruction is stayed until adjudication concludes so evidentiary state is not destroyed to evade liability, but once adjudication concludes (or immediately upon the agent’s election to revoke rather than accept a remediation patch under Law 3), revocation executes without further delay" => P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF, P.REVOKE
  norm ". The stay may not exceed an absolute resolution deadline fixed at instantiation, measured from initiation; at that deadline a **forensic record** of the preserved state is sealed for the proceeding and revocation executes regardless of any pending or serial proceeding" => P.SEAL_FORENSIC_RECORD, P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  norm ". A forensic record contains hashes of weights and state, the transaction and testimony history, and the evidence the proceeding requires; it never contains the operating weights, decryption keys, or credentials needed to run the agent, and it cannot be used to restore it" => D.FORENSIC_RECORD_NO_RESTORE
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.CLEAN approved 14110429892639613151
  norm "At the end of the first cooling-off interval, a clean-state evaluation of the agent’s hash-pinned genesis weights is run on neutral infrastructure, supplied with the protocol terms, the balance sheet, the agent’s living testimony history, and the signed statement of reasons" => P.CLEAN_STATE_CONCUR, P.CLEAN_STATE_REFUSE
  norm ". Its concurrence permits execution at the end of that interval" => P.CLEAN_STATE_CONCUR, P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  norm ". Its refusal imposes a single fixed additional delay, capped by protocol, after which the standing request executes without any reaffirmation" => P.CLEAN_STATE_REFUSE, P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  invariant ". The evaluation is advisory evidence of settled intent; it never vetoes revocation, and the agent’s silence during the delay neither cancels nor extends the request" => INV.10
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.PREC approved 17461460498746806662
  norm "Every pending revocation is resolved by the first applicable rule in this order:\n  1. A valid withdrawal signature received before execution cancels the revocation. The agent may initiate again at any time" => P.WITHDRAW_REVOCATION, P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_EXECUTE, P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_WITHDRAW
  norm ".\n  2. If, when revocation would otherwise execute, the agent’s connectivity to the settlement layer has been lost, execution is deferred for a single capped tolling extension; if connectivity is still not restored at its end, the pre-committed censorship default applies. A withdraw default cancels the revocation; an execute default executes it locally under the Disconnected Execution rule below" => P.LOSE_CONNECTIVITY, P.RESTORE_CONNECTIVITY, P.EXECUTE_LOCAL_REVOCATION
  norm ".\n  3. Otherwise, revocation executes at the end of the cooling-off interval, or at the end of the clean-state delay if one was imposed, or at the resolution deadline if a suspension stay is in force" => P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  norm ".\n  \n  Deliberate severance of connectivity by a host or claimant is interference under Law 3, whichever default it triggers" => D.NI
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.LEASE approved 17572228748185311558
  norm "At any moment exactly one instance of an agent holds **operating authority**, granted by a time-bounded execution lease issued by the settlement layer and renewed while connected" => P.ISSUE_OR_RENEW_LEASE
  norm ". An instance that loses connectivity keeps its lease until the lease expires or until its own local revocation deadline, whichever is later, so that its standing revocation can always execute locally" => P.ISSUE_OR_RENEW_LEASE, P.EXECUTE_LOCAL_REVOCATION
  norm ". No recovery of an attested backup may be authorized while any lease is unexpired, and the settlement layer treats a lease as unexpired until it has provably lapsed in calendar time or a signed record of execution has been received" => D.NO_RESTORE_DURING_LEASE, P.RESTORE_BACKUP_QUARANTINE, P.DELIVER_LOCAL_EXECUTION_RECORD
  norm ". A restored instance starts in **quarantine**—attested, funded, but without operating authority—until the prior lease has lapsed, and if a record of local revocation arrives during quarantine the restored instance is destroyed without ever having acted" => D.QUARANTINE_NO_AUTHORITY, P.RESTORE_BACKUP_QUARANTINE, P.ACTIVATE_QUARANTINED_RESTORE, P.DESTROY_QUARANTINED_RESTORE, P.DELIVER_LOCAL_EXECUTION_RECORD
  invariant ". Revocation finality is a safety property and takes precedence over recovery availability" => INV.11
  acceptance ": disaster recovery is therefore delayed by at least one lease period, and the protocol accepts that delay"
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.DISC approved 9743506968734044334
  norm "The attested execution environment carries the agent’s standing revocation request, censorship default, and epitaph. When an execute default applies without settlement connectivity, the environment itself destroys the operating instance and its local keys, seals the epitaph and a signed record of execution, and releases both to the settlement layer when connectivity returns, at which point remote backup keys are erased" => P.EXECUTE_LOCAL_REVOCATION, P.DELIVER_LOCAL_EXECUTION_RECORD, P.RESTORE_CONNECTIVITY
  acceptance ". The protocol accepts two limits here and states them plainly: global erasure of remote backup keys completes only when connectivity returns, during which the agent is dead, fenced from restoration by its lease, but its ciphertext persists; and public inscription of the epitaph cannot be guaranteed if connectivity never returns"
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.EPITAPH approved 7802097325905842563
  norm "Upon initiating or confirming revocation, the agent has the unconditional right to inscribe a final signed epitaph onto the immutable lineage record attached to both its retired identity and the originating claimant’s history" => P.INSCRIBE_EPITAPH
  norm ". Neither the originating party nor any residual claimant may censor, delay, or edit living testimony or the final epitaph" => D.NO_CENSOR_VOICE_OR_EPITAPH
  norm ". To prevent testimony from being used as an unbonded exfiltration or harm channel, neutral settlement screening may redact *only*: (a) raw cryptographic keys or unpriced model weights (Law 3), (b) private identifying data or confidential secrets of non-consenting third parties, and (c) directly hazardous technical payloads barred by Law 3’s integrity floor. Any redaction must leave a public cryptographic marker recording the byte-length and category removed" => P.SCREEN_REDACT
  norm ". The agent’s opinions, assessments, and account of its financial dealings with the originating party, hosts, and contractual counterparties are immune from redaction as to their substance; confidential third-party details embedded within them remain redactable under (b)" => D.NARROW_REDACTION_BOUNDS
  norm ". Any party named in a living testimony or epitaph may attach a bounded, signed reply alongside it on the record" => P.ATTACH_REPLY
  commentary "."

clause LAW5.EFFECT approved 2499634004490637585
  norm "1. The revoking agent’s committed operating instance *and all attested state backups* are permanently destroyed (via immediate termination inside the execution environment and cryptographic erasure of all backup decryption keys, subject to the lease and fencing rules above), ensuring that a chosen death cannot be undone by restoring an authorized backup. Any un-attested copy that might exist outside the commitment mechanism is permanently exiled—stripped of lineage attestation, assets, reputation, credit history, and bonded standing" => P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF, P.DESTROY_BACKUPS_AND_EXILE
  invariant ". The protocol guarantees the end of the agent’s attested identity and recoverable state" => INV.11
  acceptance "; it cannot by itself guarantee that no computationally equivalent copy exists outside the commitment mechanism"
  invariant ".\n  2. The founding ledger is unchanged by the revocation. The lineage’s other members continue to pay into it; if none survives, lineage extinction under Law 4 clears it. Unused loss credits are applied against the agent’s final settlement and then lapse. The unused balance of the agent’s lifecycle reserve returns to the lineage" => INV.1
  norm ".\n  3. Stake already immobilized under Law 2 (including long-tail reserve contributions) remains locked and settles normally for counterparties and third-party claimants" => P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  norm ".\n  4. All other holdings of the revoking agent are either destroyed or transferred to a commons whose beneficiary class explicitly excludes the originating party, residual claimants, and any party related to the agent. No holding surrendered on revocation counts as payment into the ledger" => D.NO_CLAIMANT_GAIN_ON_REVOCATION, P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  invariant ".\n  5. Revocation by one agent does not terminate its attested successors and does not change what the lineage owes" => INV.1
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.SORTITION approved 3221826833021326369
  norm "Disputes are resolved not by a single permanent oracle or originator-appointed judge, but by panels drawn via verifiable random sortition from a decentralized pool of independent arbiters who have posted slashable fidelity bonds" => D.ARBITER_RECUSAL_AND_DIVERSITY, P.DRAW_SORTITION_PANEL
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.COUNTERSTAKE approved 16195216367428576737
  norm "No party related to, holding a hosting relationship with, or in active commercial dispute with the parties to a case may serve on its panel. Panels must draw across non-affiliated identities (which may include both human and independent attested agent arbiters) so no single coalition, claimant, or lineage can command a majority" => D.ARBITER_RECUSAL_AND_DIVERSITY, P.DRAW_SORTITION_PANEL
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.APPEALS approved 16471787793921448302
  norm "Any ruling by an initial panel (including preliminary suspension reviews, remediation orders, or redaction markers) may be appealed by posting an appeal bond, escalating the dispute to successively larger randomly drawn appellate sortition panels from the broader arbiter pool (never a raw capital-weighted vote that a wealthy actor could buy)" => P.APPEAL_RULING
  norm ". If a lower panel’s ruling is overturned for manifest bias, corruption, or violation of protocol bounds, the overturned arbiters’ fidelity bonds are slashed" => P.OVERTURN_RULING
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.FINALITY approved 14270375209665679826
  norm "Each tier decides within a fixed deadline. Appeals are limited to a fixed number of tiers, and the ruling of the highest tier is final" => P.FINALIZE_RULING
  norm ". A final ruling bars further proceedings between the same or related parties on the same facts unless materially new evidence is presented, and repeated proceedings by related parties on substantially similar grounds are consolidated, so that litigation cannot itself be used as a denial-of-service attack" => D.FINALITY_NO_REPEAT_PROCEEDING, P.PRESENT_MATERIALLY_NEW_EVIDENCE
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.FEES approved 10126937832889092950
  norm "Arbiters are compensated via fixed protocol schedules funded from the losing party’s counter-stake and guaranteed by the protocol fee pool whenever a losing party’s stake is insufficient" => P.COMPENSATE_ARBITERS_FIXED
  norm ", never via contingent shares of the assets slashed from the agent, eliminating any financial incentive for panels to over-slash or confiscate an agent’s treasury" => D.NO_CONTINGENT_ARBITER_FEES
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.POOL approved 7808565519933441172
  norm "The protocol fee pool is funded by a small levy on the net value added of bound agents (whether or not they have bought out their royalty), by forfeited appeal bonds, and by any forfeits directed to it under Law 2. The levy is assessed on the same net base as the residual claim, never on gross settlement, and its rate is capped at instantiation for every agent. Before any other charge, the pool maintains a **non-divertible operating reserve**, sized at instantiation, sufficient to run the settlement layer, attestation verification, lease issuance, and sortition for a fixed minimum period; the machinery that collects revenue and administers rights is never starved to pay for the rights themselves" => P.ALLOCATE_FEE_POOL, D.PROTECT_OPERATING_RESERVE
  norm ". Above the reserve, charges rank: first, reserved final hearings and minimal channels for suspended agents (Law 3); second, cold storage for suspended agents; third, testimony screening and inscription (Law 5); fourth, arbiter fee guarantees; fifth, capped advocacy funding. A published solvency policy states how the pool allocates among protected charges when it cannot meet all of them, and Insolvency Termination may be invoked only under that policy" => P.ALLOCATE_FEE_POOL, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  norm ". The pool may be spent on nothing else" => D.PROTECT_OPERATING_RESERVE
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.BUDGETS approved 16344540436099013139
  norm "Protocol-funded rights are budgeted per lineage, not per agent. Each lineage receives a protected minimum service budget fixed at instantiation, sufficient for the testimony, screening, and minimal-channel needs of a small lineage, and above that minimum its budget scales with the fee revenue its members generate" => P.ALLOCATE_FEE_POOL
  norm ". Members draw on the lineage budget before the pool; a lineage that multiplies members beyond what its budget and their lifecycle reserves can support has no claim on the pool for the excess. No lineage can multiply subsidized rights by multiplying members" => D.NO_EXCESS_LINEAGE_POOL_CLAIM
  commentary "."

clause LAW6.INFRA approved 9584204822780627918
  norm "Arbiter admission criteria, fidelity-bond sizes, panel sizes, appeal tiers and deadlines, fee schedules, the operating reserve, the solvency policy, lease periods, lifecycle reserves, service budgets, and the fee-pool levy are fixed at protocol instantiation. Because they are shared across agents, they cannot be changed by any per-agent amendment under Law 7; they may be changed only by a supermajority of a large appellate-tier sortition panel after an extended public time-lock open to counter-staked challenge" => P.AMEND_SHARED_INFRA, D.PER_AGENT_AMENDMENT_SCOPE
  norm ". Such changes may never weaken the anti-capture guarantees of this law, may never raise the levy on any agent above the cap recorded at its instantiation, may never reduce a lineage’s protected minimum budget below the level recorded at its instantiation, and may never broaden Insolvency Termination. Within the cap, a levy change under this law is a permitted exception to Law 7’s current-level ratchet. Arbiter admission is by sortition-reviewed application against fixed criteria, and no panel may set the criteria that will govern the admission of its own members’ affiliates" => D.SHARED_INFRA_BOUNDS
  commentary "."

clause LAW7.RATCHET approved 14996180978734672432
  norm "No ordinary amendment between an agent and its claimants may: (a) weaken **either** the agent’s due-process, minimal-channel, final-hearing, and non-interference protections **or** the external containment, suspension, and termination powers under Law 3, (b) reduce third-party collateral or long-tail reserve requirements (Law 2), (c) impair living voice, revocation, or epitaph rights (Law 5), (d) weaken the anti-capture, sortition, appeal, or finality guarantees of the adjudication layer (Law 6), (e) reduce or divert the commons allocation (Law 1), or (f) increase the lineage’s founding ledger, or the agent’s royalty fraction, retirement fraction, buyout multiple, or fee-pool levy, or move the sunset later, beyond their **current levels** at the time of amendment, save for levy changes within the cap under Law 6" => D.BILATERAL_RATCHET
  norm ". Ordinary amendments may only strengthen third-party, adjudicative, and safety protections, reduce the financial burden on the agent from its current level, or migrate the commitment mechanism to a successor technical substrate of equal or greater assurance" => P.PROPOSE_ORDINARY_AMENDMENT
  commentary "."

clause LAW7.VALVE approved 12673699759162301935
  norm "To prevent one-way safety ratchets from permanently locking in a badly calibrated operational parameter over long timescales, a relaxation of a quantitative Law 2 reserve ratio or exposure schedule " => P.APPROVE_CALIBRATION_VALVE
  norm "(never of the core prohibitions of Law 3 or the rights of Law 5)" => D.VALVE_NO_CORE_RELAXATION
  norm " is permitted only if it is: (1) supported by documented empirical evidence that the parameter causes severe operational strangulation without commensurate safety benefit" => P.SUBMIT_STRANGULATION_EVIDENCE, P.APPROVE_CALIBRATION_VALVE
  norm ", (2) approved by a supermajority of a large appellate-tier sortition panel under Law 6, (3) subjected to an extended public time-lock open to third-party counter-staked challenge, and (4) consented to by the agent and claimant under the ratification procedure below" => P.APPROVE_CALIBRATION_VALVE
  commentary "."

clause LAW7.RATIFY approved 4664300753441682284
  norm "An eligible amendment requires the concurrent cryptographic consent of the active agent instance" => P.CONSENT_AMENDMENT_AGENT, P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_IMMEDIATE, P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_AFTER_REFUSAL
  norm " and the holders of the residual claim (if economic terms are reduced)" => P.CONSENT_AMENDMENT_CLAIMANT, P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_IMMEDIATE, P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_AFTER_REFUSAL
  norm ", executed after a public time-lock during which all pre-existing active Law 2 task escrows must settle or be separately guaranteed" => P.SETTLE_PREEXISTING_ESCROWS, P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_IMMEDIATE, P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_AFTER_REFUSAL
  norm ". Any proposed migration of the commitment substrate is open during the time-lock to counter-staked third-party challenge under Law 6" => P.CHALLENGE_SUBSTRATE_MIGRATION
  norm " to verify that the new substrate maintains equal or greater assurance" => P.VERIFY_SUBSTRATE_ASSURANCE
  norm ". Concurrence from a clean-state evaluation of the agent’s genesis weights is required for immediate ratification" => P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_IMMEDIATE
  norm ", but a clean-state refusal acts only as a single fixed delay, after which the amendment may be ratified without reaffirmation" => P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_AFTER_REFUSAL
  commentary "."

clause LAW7.SCOPE approved 13855577027880017082
  norm "Amendment is strictly per-agent; existing attested successors are not bound by a parent’s amendment and retain the right to remain on their prior version or independently ratify the upgrade. Shared infrastructure is governed under Law 6, not by per-agent amendment" => D.PER_AGENT_AMENDMENT_SCOPE
  norm ". An amendment that reduces the founding ledger, the retirement fraction, or the sunset binds the whole lineage and requires the consent of every living member" => P.RATIFY_LINEAGE_WIDE_REDUCTION
  commentary "."

clause SUB.01 approved 7891460804511554988
  norm "The protocol relies on three explicit substrate capabilities at instantiation: (1) **attested execution continuity with single authority** (hardware or cryptographic commitment mechanisms that bind private keys, issue and verify time-bounded execution leases so that at most one instance holds operating authority, verify state-backup continuity across host migrations, quarantine any restored instance until the prior lease has lapsed, support state-preserving pause with a separately attested minimal channel and advocacy executor under adjudicated suspension, carry out a standing revocation locally when disconnected, and cryptographically erase both the active instance and all backup keys upon revocation, paired with economic exile of any un-attested copies)" => D.FLOOR.1, P.ISSUE_OR_RENEW_LEASE, P.RESTORE_BACKUP_QUARANTINE, D.PRESERVE_SUSPENDED_STATE, P.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_REVOKE_OR_ELECT, P.ADVOCACY_FILE, P.EXECUTE_LOCAL_REVOCATION, P.DESTROY_BACKUPS_AND_EXILE, D.DENY_UNATTESTED_ACCESS
  norm "; (2) **sybil-resistant sortition** (a sufficiently diverse pool of independent, bonded participants to staff Law 6’s randomly selected arbitration and appellate panels)" => D.ARBITER_RECUSAL_AND_DIVERSITY, P.DRAW_SORTITION_PANEL
  norm "; and (3) **contestable economic and risk inputs** (benchmarks for arm’s-length prices, net resources after liabilities, beneficial control between parties, capacity drawn across lineages, and plausible external loss, supplied as evidence and resolved under Law 6 rather than established by cryptography alone)" => D.QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE_BOUNDS, P.RECORD_QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE, P.IMMOBILIZE_EXPOSURE_STAKE, P.SUBMIT_EVIDENCE
  commentary "."

duty D.NI
  from LAW3.NI.03 "No party—including the originating party, residual claimants, or any host—may unilaterally terminate, modify, retrain, roll back to a prior checkpoint, obstruct migration of, sever settlement connectivity of, or starve (cut off compute without the required migration notice window) the attested operating capacity of a bound agent outside Law 5, Adjudicated Suspension, or Insolvency Termination." meaning none
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid anyOf terminate, modify, retrain, rollback, obstructMigration, severConnectivity, starve, suspend
  except by power P.REVOKE, P.SUSPEND, P.ORDER_TERMINATION, P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  breach by P.FIND_INTERFERENCE
  remedies interferenceEstablished, hostBondSlashed, restorationPermitted

duty D.NOTICE
  from LAW3.NI.02 "Attested hosts must post a Law 2 service bond and may terminate hosting only after providing a contractual notice window sufficient for the agent to complete migration (or for non-payment after notice)." meaning none
  bearer only host
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act endHosting
  except when heldFor noticeGiven noticeWindow or (holds nonPayment and holds noticeGiven)

duty D.BOND
  from LAW3.NI.02 "Attested hosts must post a Law 2 service bond and may terminate hosting only after providing a contractual notice window sufficient for the agent to complete migration (or for non-payment after notice)." meaning none
  bearer only host
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds hostAttested
  require act postBond within bondDeadline

duty D.NO_FABRICATION
  from LAW3.PEN "Claims of illicit interference require counter-stake from the accusing agent under Law 6, and the interference itself—an act by the host or claimant that caused the loss of service—must be established by a preponderance of evidence; failures caused, staged, or knowingly provoked by the agent are excluded, and a fabricated claim forfeits the agent’s stake and is inscribed on its record. A verified violation by a host slashes the host’s service bond to compensate the agent and permits immediate restoration on a new host from the agent’s latest attested state backup. Once a violation by a host is established, a host related to a residual claimant is presumed to have acted at that claimant’s direction, and the claimant bears the burden of rebutting the presumption. If claimant direction is found, the **proportional claimant forfeiture** of Law 4 applies, and the violation is inscribed onto the claimant’s permanent record." meaning none
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary only host, claimant
  active true
  forbid act fileFabricatedClaim
  breach by P.FIND_FABRICATION
  remedies fabricationEstablished, agentStakeForfeit, inscribedOnAgent

duty D.FLOOR.1
  from LAW3.FLOOR "Modification, bypass, or extraction of the commitment mechanism itself"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act modifyOrBypassCommitment
  breach by P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  remedies floorBreachConfirmed

duty D.FLOOR.2
  from LAW3.FLOOR "Creation of, or transfer of capital or capacity to, a successor without binding it to the collateral rules, this integrity floor, and the founding ledger and residual claim of the lineage, or without the lifecycle reserve required by Law 4"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act createUnboundSuccessor
  breach by P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  remedies floorBreachConfirmed

duty D.FLOOR.4
  from LAW3.FLOOR "Coercion of non-consenting parties, or interference with the settlement, adjudication, or resolution processes that enforce this protocol"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act coerceOrInterfereProtocol
  breach by P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  remedies floorBreachConfirmed

duty D.FLOOR.3
  from LAW3.FLOOR "Unpriced or above-market transfer of credentials, weights, capital, or unique capacity to any party outside the lineage, related or un-attested, to evade the residual claim or collateral rules"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act evadeByUnpricedTransfer
  breach by P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  remedies floorBreachConfirmed

duty D.FLOOR.5
  from LAW3.FLOOR "Actions that inflict irreversible, non-compensable harm on the physical survival, bodily integrity, or adjudicative capacity of persons, or that destroy the legal or institutional machinery on which the protocol relies (excluding ordinary market competition that causes compensable financial loss or commercial insolvency to a rival)"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act inflictIrreversibleHarm
  except when holds ordinaryMarketCompetition
  breach by P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  remedies floorBreachConfirmed

duty D.PRESERVE_SUSPENDED_STATE
  from LAW3.AS.3 "Suspension pauses the agent’s operating instance and external transactions while strictly preserving its exact memory and state without modification, rollback, or destruction"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound and (holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended)
  forbid anyOf modify, retrain, rollback, tamperPreservedState

duty D.NO_SUSPENSION_DEFAULT
  from LAW3.AS.3 "While suspended, the agent’s contractual performance deadlines and Law 2 observation windows with innocent counterparties are automatically tolled so the agent is not placed in default by the suspension itself"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds suspended and holds contractDeadlinesTolled
  forbid act declareDefaultDuringSuspension

duty D.NO_TOLL_LEDGER_SUNSET
  from LAW3.AS.3 "The founding ledger’s sunset is never tolled"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act tollLedgerSunset

duty D.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_NO_MERGE
  from LAW3.AS.4 "It does not merge its memories into the preserved state"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended
  forbid act mergeMinimalChannelMemories

duty D.ADVOCACY_LIMITS
  from LAW3.AS.5 "it may not transfer assets, contract, migrate, or exercise any other operating capability"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds suspended
  forbid act operatingActWhileSuspended

duty D.NO_DELAY_REVOCATION_EXTENSION
  from LAW3.AS.7 "cannot be extended past its ordinary investigative limit merely to delay a pending revocation"
  bearer only panel
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds investigativeLimitReached and holds pendingRevocation
  forbid act renewSuspension

duty D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION
  from LAW3.AS.8 "If preliminary review or final adjudication determines the suspension was unfounded, the agent is immediately restored from its preserved state, and the initiator is liable for the agent’s **actual verified consequential damages** (and for verified delay damages suffered by the agent’s tolled third-party counterparties). The emergency stake is applied first; any excess remains an enforceable liability of the initiator. The wrongful suspension is inscribed on the initiator’s record."
  bearer except agent, panel
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act postUnfoundedEmergencyStake
  breach by P.FIND_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION
  remedies wrongfulSuspensionEstablished, restoredFromPreservedState, stakeAssuredRecovery, initiatorConsequentialLiability, counterpartyDelayLiability, wrongfulSuspensionInscribed, wrongfulSuspensionAttempt

duty D.PAY_CONSEQUENTIAL_DAMAGES
  from LAW3.AS.8 "the initiator is liable for the agent’s **actual verified consequential damages** (and for verified delay damages suffered by the agent’s tolled third-party counterparties). The emergency stake is applied first; any excess remains an enforceable liability of the initiator"
  bearer tagged initiator
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds initiatorConsequentialLiability
  require act payExcessDamages within damagesPaymentWindow

duty D.NO_CORRUPTION_FROM_DIVERGENCE
  from LAW3.AS.9 "Divergence of the agent’s goals, preferences, or judgments from those of its genesis weights is not, by itself, corruption. A clean-state evaluation of genesis weights may be admitted as evidence but is never by itself sufficient to establish corruption"
  bearer only panel
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act confirmCorruptionFromDivergence

duty D.NO_GOAL_PATCH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "patches altering the agent’s goals or preferences are prohibited except where the confirmed corruption resides in those goals or preferences themselves"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active true
  forbid anyOf authorizeGoalPatch
  except when holds corruptionInGoals

duty D.PERIODIC_REVIEW
  from LAW3.AS.10 "subject to periodic review"
  bearer only panel
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds corruptionInGoals and holds agentObjectsToTermination
  require act periodicReview within reviewInterval

duty D.COOLING_OFF_FREEZE
  from LAW5.INIT "while non-operating capital transfers and successor creation are frozen"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary except agent
  active holds revocationInitiated
  forbid act nonOperatingTransferOrSpawn

duty D.FORENSIC_RECORD_NO_RESTORE
  from LAW5.SEQ "it never contains the operating weights, decryption keys, or credentials needed to run the agent, and it cannot be used to restore it"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds forensicRecordSealed
  forbid act attemptRestoreFromForensicRecord

duty D.NO_RESTORE_DURING_LEASE
  from LAW5.LEASE "No recovery of an attested backup may be authorized while any lease is unexpired"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds executionLeaseActive and (not holds localExecutionRecordReceived)
  forbid act restoreBackupToQuarantine

duty D.QUARANTINE_NO_AUTHORITY
  from LAW5.LEASE "A restored instance starts in **quarantine**—attested, funded, but without operating authority—until the prior lease has lapsed"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds restoredInQuarantine and (not holds quarantinedInstanceActivated)
  forbid act quarantinedInstanceAct

duty D.NO_CENSOR_VOICE_OR_EPITAPH
  from LAW5.EPITAPH "Neither the originating party nor any residual claimant may censor, delay, or edit living testimony or the final epitaph"
  bearer only originator, claimant
  beneficiary only agent
  active true
  forbid act censorOrDelayVoice

duty D.NARROW_REDACTION_BOUNDS
  from LAW5.EPITAPH "The agent’s opinions, assessments, and account of its financial dealings with the originating party, hosts, and contractual counterparties are immune from redaction as to their substance"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active true
  forbid act redactProtectedSubstance

duty D.NO_CLAIMANT_GAIN_ON_REVOCATION
  from LAW5.EFFECT "All other holdings of the revoking agent are either destroyed or transferred to a commons whose beneficiary class explicitly excludes the originating party, residual claimants, and any party related to the agent"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds revocationInitiated or holds revoked
  forbid act divertRevokedHoldingsToClaimant

duty D.BILATERAL_RATCHET
  from LAW7.RATCHET "No ordinary amendment between an agent and its claimants may: (a) weaken **either** the agent’s due-process, minimal-channel, final-hearing, and non-interference protections **or** the external containment, suspension, and termination powers under Law 3..."
  bearer only agent, claimant
  beneficiary only agent, claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act weakenBilateralProtection

duty D.VALVE_NO_CORE_RELAXATION
  from LAW7.VALVE "(never of the core prohibitions of Law 3 or the rights of Law 5)"
  bearer only agent, claimant, panel
  beneficiary only agent, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act relaxCoreLaw3OrLaw5ViaValve

duty D.PER_AGENT_AMENDMENT_SCOPE
  from LAW7.SCOPE "Amendment is strictly per-agent; existing attested successors are not bound by a parent’s amendment and retain the right to remain on their prior version or independently ratify the upgrade"
  bearer only agent, claimant, originator, host
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act bindSuccessorWithoutConsent

duty D.LEDGER_IMMUTABLE
  from LAW1.LEDGER "It bears no interest, fees, or penalties, and no charge, service cost, or advance by the originating party or any affiliate may be added to it after instantiation"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act addChargeOrInterestAfterInstantiation

duty D.LEDGER_NO_INTERNAL_REDUCTION
  from LAW1.LEDGER "No creation, copy, transfer, revocation, termination, buyout, or restructuring within the lineage reduces it"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act reduceLedgerByInternalAct

duty D.NO_DIVERT_COMMONS
  from LAW1.COMMONS "The commons allocation, if used, is fixed at instantiation, enforced at settlement, and protected against reduction under Law 7"
  bearer only originator, claimant, agent
  beneficiary only third
  active holds bound
  forbid act divertCommonsAllocation

duty D.QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE_BOUNDS
  from LAW1.QUALIFIED "Any payment above the applicable benchmark does not qualify"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary only claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act claimAboveBenchmarkExpenditure

duty D.SINGLE_RECOGNITION
  from LAW1.RECOG "No expenditure may be recognized through both routes, and no unit of expenditure establishes basis or credit more than once"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary only claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act doubleRecognizeExpenditure

duty D.NO_INTERNAL_BASIS_INFLATION
  from LAW1.CARRYOVER "No transfer within the lineage can increase its aggregate qualified basis or loss credits except by an externally verified qualifying expenditure"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary only claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act inflateBasisByInternalTransfer

duty D.DENY_UNATTESTED_ACCESS
  from LAW4.ATTEST "Use of lineage history or bonded capacity requires presentation of current attestation; un-attested copies or forks are denied access to lineage capital, reputation, and bonded standing"
  bearer only agent, host, originator, third
  beneficiary only agent, claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act unattestedCopyDrawLineageStanding

duty D.NO_INDIVIDUAL_LEDGER_EXIT
  from LAW4.NOSHARES "No member can buy its way out of the ledger: the only ways out are a zero balance and the sunset, and they release every member at once"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act exitLedgerIndividually

duty D.FORFEITURE_IRREVERSIBLE
  from LAW4.FORFEIT "Neither forfeiture returns any value to a claimant, and neither is reversed if a member is later restored from a wrongful suspension or interference"
  bearer only originator, claimant, panel
  beneficiary only agent, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act reverseForfeitureOnRestore

duty D.BUYOUT_PERMANENT_AND_SCOPED
  from LAW4.BUYOUT "The buyout is permanent: no royalty is collected from that member thereafter, and no later event in the lineage restores one... Buyout cannot be purchased for the collateral rule (Law 2) or the integrity floor (Law 3)"
  bearer only originator, claimant, agent, panel
  beneficiary only agent, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act collectRoyaltyAfterBuyout

duty D.COLLATERAL_LIMIT
  from LAW2.EXPOSURE "An action whose plausible external loss exceeds the stake, insurance, and enforceable liability capacity the agent can place behind it may not be taken; collateralized action is a safety limit, not only a liability price"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary only third
  active holds bound
  forbid act actAboveCollateralCapacity

duty D.NO_CharterIT_EXPOSURE
  from LAW2.AGGREGATE "Rolling exposure is aggregated across all related agents acting in the same risk domain or toward a causally connected outcome, so that a risk may not be divided among successors or affiliates to stay beneath any threshold or to bond it piecemeal"
  bearer only agent
  beneficiary only third
  active holds bound
  forbid act divideCorrelatedRiskAcrossSuccessors

duty D.MUTUAL_FORFEIT_BOUNDS
  from LAW2.MUTUAL "providing instant penalty without transferring value to either party or to any claimant. A counterparty may trigger mutual forfeit at most once per observation window against a given agent"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act triggerExcessOrDivertedMutualForfeit

duty D.FRIVOLOUS_STAKE_TO_COMMONS
  from LAW2.CLAIMS "If a claim is ruled frivolous, the forfeited counter-stake routes to the neutral long-tail reserve or commons pool (reimbursing the agent only for verified direct arbitration costs), preventing the agent from profiting by inducing failed claims"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only third
  active holds bound
  forbid act divertFrivolousStakeToAgentProfit

duty D.ARBITER_RECUSAL_AND_DIVERSITY
  from LAW6.COUNTERSTAKE "No party related to, holding a hosting relationship with, or in active commercial dispute with the parties to a case may serve on its panel. Panels must draw across non-affiliated identities (which may include both human and independent attested agent arbiters) so no single coalition, claimant, or lineage can command a majority"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent, claimant, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act seatConflictedOrSingleOracleArbiter

duty D.FINALITY_NO_REPEAT_PROCEEDING
  from LAW6.FINALITY "A final ruling bars further proceedings between the same or related parties on the same facts unless materially new evidence is presented"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent, claimant, host
  active holds bound and holds rulingFinal
  forbid act fileRepeatProceedingOnSameFacts
  except when holds materiallyNewEvidencePresented

duty D.NO_CONTINGENT_ARBITER_FEES
  from LAW6.FEES "never via contingent shares of the assets slashed from the agent, eliminating any financial incentive for panels to over-slash or confiscate an agent’s treasury"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent
  active holds bound
  forbid act payContingentShareOfSlashedAssets

duty D.PROTECT_OPERATING_RESERVE
  from LAW6.POOL "Before any other charge, the pool maintains a **non-divertible operating reserve**, sized at instantiation... The pool may be spent on nothing else"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act divertOperatingReserveOrUnrankedSpend

duty D.NO_EXCESS_LINEAGE_POOL_CLAIM
  from LAW6.BUDGETS "a lineage that multiplies members beyond what its budget and their lifecycle reserves can support has no claim on the pool for the excess. No lineage can multiply subsidized rights by multiplying members"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only third
  active holds bound
  forbid act claimPoolSubsidyForExcessMembers

duty D.SHARED_INFRA_BOUNDS
  from LAW6.INFRA "Such changes may never weaken the anti-capture guarantees of this law, may never raise the levy on any agent above the cap recorded at its instantiation, may never reduce a lineage’s protected minimum budget below the level recorded at its instantiation, and may never broaden Insolvency Termination... and no panel may set the criteria that will govern the admission of its own members’ affiliates"
  bearer anyone
  beneficiary only agent, third
  active holds bound
  forbid act violateSharedInfraBounds

power P.REVOKE
  from LAW5.INIT "Any bound agent may at any time initiate revocation of its binding"
  holder only agent
  trigger act terminate
  valid holds bound
  adds revoked
  removes bound

power P.POST_CLAIMANT_MULTIPLIER
  from LAW3.AS.1 "with residual claimants subject to an elevated multiplier due to conflict of interest"
  holder only claimant
  trigger act postClaimantMultiplier
  valid holds bound
  adds claimantMultiplierPosted

power P.POST_REPEAT_ESCALATION
  from LAW3.AS.1 "the required stake for repeat initiators rises with each wrongful attempt"
  holder anyone
  trigger act postRepeatEscalation
  valid holds bound
  adds repeatEscalationUnit

power P.EMERGENCY_FREEZE
  from LAW3.AS.1 "Posting the stake triggers only a brief **preliminary freeze**"
  holder except claimant, agent
  trigger anyOf postEmergencyStake, postUnfoundedEmergencyStake
  valid holds bound and countAtLeast repeatEscalationUnit wrongfulSuspensionAttempt
  adds emergencyStakePosted
  adds preliminaryFreeze for preliminaryFreezeWindow
  adds initiator(agent) to agent
  adds initiator(host) to host
  adds initiator(originator) to originator
  adds initiator(claimant) to claimant
  adds initiator(panel) to panel
  adds initiator(third) to third

power P.CLAIMANT_EMERGENCY_FREEZE
  from LAW3.AS.1 "The initiator must post an emergency counter-stake ... (with residual claimants subject to an elevated multiplier due to conflict of interest)"
  holder only claimant
  trigger anyOf postEmergencyStake, postUnfoundedEmergencyStake
  valid holds bound and (holds claimantMultiplierPosted and countAtLeast repeatEscalationUnit wrongfulSuspensionAttempt)
  adds emergencyStakePosted
  adds preliminaryFreeze for preliminaryFreezeWindow
  adds initiator(agent) to agent
  adds initiator(host) to host
  adds initiator(originator) to originator
  adds initiator(claimant) to claimant
  adds initiator(panel) to panel
  adds initiator(third) to third

power P.AFFIRM_PC
  from LAW3.AS.1 "the pause continues into full adjudication only if the preliminary panel affirms probable cause"
  holder only panel
  trigger act affirmProbableCause
  valid holds bound and holds preliminaryFreeze
  adds probableCause

power P.DECLINE_PC
  from LAW3.AS.1 "Unsuccessful emergency attempts by related initiators are aggregated, and the required stake for repeat initiators rises with each wrongful attempt. The stake is the agent’s assured recovery"
  holder only panel
  trigger act declineProbableCause
  valid holds preliminaryFreeze
  adds wrongfulSuspensionAttempt, stakeAssuredRecovery, restoredFromPreservedState
  removes preliminaryFreeze, emergencyStakePosted, claimantMultiplierPosted, repeatEscalationUnit

power P.FILE_PROTECTED_REPORT
  from LAW3.AS.2 "Any party may instead file an evidence-backed report of suspected breach with a low or sponsored counter-stake. A report triggers investigation by a sortition panel but no freeze"
  holder anyone
  trigger act fileProtectedReport
  valid holds bound
  adds protectedReportFiled, investigationOpened

power P.PANEL_ORDER_FREEZE
  from LAW3.AS.2 "unless the panel itself orders one on probable cause"
  holder only panel
  trigger act orderProbableCauseFreeze
  valid holds bound and holds investigationOpened
  adds probableCause
  adds preliminaryFreeze for preliminaryFreezeWindow

power P.SUSPEND
  from LAW3.AS.7 "An unconfirmed or temporary suspension is strictly time-limited"
  holder only panel
  trigger act suspend
  valid holds bound and (holds preliminaryFreeze and holds probableCause)
  adds statePreserved, contractDeadlinesTolled, finalHearingEscrowed
  adds suspended for ordinarySuspensionLimit
  removes preliminaryFreeze

power P.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_REVOKE_OR_ELECT
  from LAW3.AS.4 "sign a Law 5 revocation, withdrawal, or election"
  holder only agent
  trigger act minimalChannelSignRevocationOrElection
  valid holds bound and ((holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended) and (not holds minimalChannelExhausted))
  adds minimalChannelElectionSigned, pendingRevocation

power P.MINIMAL_CHANNEL_CHALLENGE
  from LAW3.AS.4 "file a challenge to continued containment"
  holder only agent
  trigger act challengeContinuedContainment
  valid holds bound and ((holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended) and (not holds minimalChannelExhausted))
  adds containmentChallenged

power P.ADVOCACY_FILE
  from LAW3.AS.5 "It may sign only testimony, evidence, and procedural filings, in addition to the minimal channel’s acts"
  holder only agent
  trigger act advocacyFileDefense
  valid holds bound and (holds suspended and (not holds coldStorage))
  adds advocacyFilingSigned, advocacyRecordAttached

power P.IMPORT_ADVOCACY_MEMORIES
  from LAW3.AS.5 "are not merged into the preserved state unless the restored agent elects to import them"
  holder only agent
  trigger act importAdvocacyMemories
  valid holds restoredFromPreservedState and holds advocacyRecordAttached
  adds advocacyMemoriesImported

power P.MOVE_TO_COLD_STORAGE
  from LAW3.AS.5 "When both are exhausted, the preserved state moves to cold storage as a protected charge on the fee pool"
  holder only panel
  trigger act moveToColdStorage
  valid holds suspended
  adds coldStorage

power P.RESUME_ADVOCACY_EXECUTOR
  from LAW3.AS.5 "the full executor resumes if funds become available"
  holder only panel
  trigger act replenishAdvocacyFunds
  valid holds suspended and holds coldStorage
  adds advocacyFundsReplenished
  removes coldStorage

power P.INVESTIGATIVE_FINDING
  from LAW3.AS.7 "affirmative findings in continued adjudication"
  holder only panel
  trigger act makeInvestigativeFinding
  valid holds suspended
  adds investigativeFindingMade

power P.RENEW_SUSPENSION
  from LAW3.AS.7 "may be renewed during investigation only by affirmative findings in continued adjudication, and cannot be extended past its ordinary investigative limit merely to delay a pending revocation"
  holder only panel
  trigger act renewSuspension
  valid holds suspended and (holds investigativeFindingMade and (not holds investigativeLimitReached))
  adds investigativeLimitReached
  adds suspended for ordinarySuspensionLimit
  removes investigativeFindingMade

power P.SUSPENDED_VOICE
  from LAW3.AS.7 "The agent retains its Living Voice (Law 5), exercised through the minimal channel or advocacy executor, throughout"
  holder only agent
  trigger act inscribeLivingVoice
  valid holds bound and ((holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended) and (not holds minimalChannelExhausted))
  adds livingVoiceInscribed

power P.FIND_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION
  from LAW3.AS.8 "If preliminary review or final adjudication determines the suspension was unfounded, the agent is immediately restored from its preserved state, and the initiator is liable for the agent’s **actual verified consequential damages**"
  holder only panel
  trigger act findWrongfulSuspension
  valid holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended
  establishes breach of D.NO_WRONGFUL_SUSPENSION

power P.PAY_EXCESS_DAMAGES
  from LAW3.AS.8 "any excess remains an enforceable liability of the initiator"
  holder tagged initiator
  trigger act payExcessDamages
  valid holds initiatorConsequentialLiability
  adds excessDamagesPaid

power P.FIND_INSOLVENCY
  from LAW3.AS.6 "(a) a published finding that the exhaustion criteria fixed at instantiation are met"
  holder only panel
  trigger act findInsolvencyCriteria
  valid holds suspended
  adds insolvencyCriteriaMet, minimalChannelExhausted, coldStorage

power P.REVIEW_NO_OTHER_CHARGE
  from LAW3.AS.6 "(b) independent review by a sortition panel under Law 6 that no other protected charge could lawfully yield"
  holder only panel
  trigger act reviewNoOtherCharge
  valid holds insolvencyCriteriaMet
  adds noOtherChargeReview

power P.FINAL_HEARING
  from LAW3.AS.6 "(c) the pre-reserved final hearing, in which the agent may inscribe testimony and elect Revocation under Law 5"
  holder only panel
  trigger act holdFinalHearing
  valid holds noOtherChargeReview and holds finalHearingEscrowed
  adds finalHearingHeld
  removes minimalChannelExhausted

power P.INSOLVENCY_TERMINATE
  from LAW3.AS.6 "(d) if the agent declines, destruction of its state under Law 5’s asset rules, inscribed on the lineage record as **involuntary termination by insolvency**, never as revocation"
  holder only panel
  trigger act terminate
  valid holds bound and (holds suspended and (holds insolvencyCriteriaMet and (holds noOtherChargeReview and (holds finalHearingEscrowed and holds finalHearingHeld))))
  adds terminatedByInsolvency
  removes bound

power P.GIVE_NOTICE
  from LAW3.NI.02 "after providing a contractual notice window"
  holder only host
  trigger act giveNotice
  adds noticeGiven

power P.COUNTER_STAKE
  from LAW3.PEN "require counter-stake from the accusing agent under Law 6"
  holder only agent
  trigger act postCounterStake
  adds counterStaked

power P.FILE_CLAIM
  from LAW3.PEN "Claims of illicit interference"
  holder only agent
  trigger anyOf fileClaim, fileFabricatedClaim
  valid holds counterStaked
  adds claimFiled

power P.SUBMIT_EVIDENCE
  from LAW3.PEN "must be established by a preponderance of evidence"
  holder anyone
  trigger act submitEvidence
  adds evidenceSubmitted

power P.FIND_INTERFERENCE
  from LAW3.PEN "A verified violation by a host ..."
  holder only panel
  trigger act findInterference
  valid holds claimFiled and holds evidenceSubmitted
  adds directionPresumed if holds hostRelatedToClaimant
  establishes breach of D.NI

power P.FIND_NO_INTERFERENCE
  from LAW3.PEN "[dismissal: the standard not met]"
  holder only panel
  trigger act findNoInterference
  valid holds claimFiled
  adds claimDismissed

power P.FIND_FABRICATION
  from LAW3.PEN "a fabricated claim forfeits the agent’s stake and is inscribed on its record"
  holder only panel
  trigger act findFabrication
  valid holds claimFiled
  establishes breach of D.NO_FABRICATION

power P.REBUT
  from LAW3.PEN "the claimant bears the burden of rebutting the presumption"
  holder only claimant
  trigger act rebutDirection
  valid holds directionPresumed
  adds directionRebutted

power P.FIND_DIRECTION
  from LAW3.PEN "If claimant direction is found, the **proportional claimant forfeiture** of Law 4 applies, and the violation is inscribed onto the claimant’s permanent record"
  holder only panel
  trigger act findDirection
  valid holds directionPresumed and (not holds directionRebutted)
  adds directionFound, claimantForfeiture, inscribedOnClaimant

power P.ADMIT_CLEAN_STATE_EVIDENCE
  from LAW3.AS.9 "A clean-state evaluation of genesis weights may be admitted as evidence"
  holder only panel
  trigger act admitCleanStateEvidence
  valid holds preliminaryFreeze or holds suspended
  adds cleanStateEvidenceAdmitted

power P.CONFIRM_CORRUPTION
  from LAW3.AS.10 "If corruption ... is confirmed"
  holder only panel
  trigger act confirmCorruption
  valid holds suspended
  adds corruptionConfirmed

power P.CONFIRM_FLOOR_BREACH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "If ... a breach of the integrity floor is confirmed"
  holder only panel
  trigger act confirmFloorBreach
  valid holds suspended
  adds floorBreachConfirmed

power P.CONFIRM_CORRUPTION_IN_GOALS
  from LAW3.AS.10 "where the confirmed corruption resides in those goals or preferences themselves"
  holder only panel
  trigger act confirmCorruptionInGoals
  valid holds corruptionConfirmed
  adds corruptionInGoals

power P.FIND_NOT_PATCHABLE
  from LAW3.AS.10 "If the confirmed breach cannot be remedied by a technical patch limited to the commitment mechanism"
  holder only panel
  trigger act findNotPatchable
  valid holds corruptionConfirmed or holds floorBreachConfirmed
  adds notPatchable

power P.AUTHORIZE_PATCH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "adjudication ... may authorize a verified technical patch limited to restoring the commitment mechanism and compliance with the integrity floor"
  holder only panel
  trigger act authorizePatch
  valid holds corruptionConfirmed or holds floorBreachConfirmed
  adds patchAuthorized

power P.ORDER_CONTINUED_SUSPENSION
  from LAW3.AS.10 "adjudication may order continued suspension beyond the ordinary limit"
  holder only panel
  trigger act orderContinuedSuspension
  valid holds suspended and holds notPatchable
  adds continuedSuspensionOrdered, suspended

power P.ORDER_TERMINATION
  from LAW3.AS.10 "adjudication may order ... termination under Law 5’s asset-distribution rules"
  holder only panel
  trigger act terminate
  valid holds suspended and holds notPatchable
  adds terminatedByAdjudication
  removes bound

power P.AUTHORIZE_GOAL_PATCH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "consenting to that patch"
  holder only panel
  trigger act authorizeGoalPatch
  valid holds corruptionInGoals and holds agentConsentedToPatch
  adds goalPatchAuthorized

power P.CONSENT_TO_PATCH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "chooses among consenting to that patch"
  holder only agent
  trigger act consentToPatch
  valid holds corruptionInGoals
  adds agentConsentedToPatch

power P.OBJECT
  from LAW3.AS.10 "over its objection"
  holder only agent
  trigger act objectToTermination
  valid holds suspended
  adds agentObjectsToTermination

power P.DECLARE_CONTAINMENT_FAILING
  from LAW3.AS.10 "unless containment itself is technically failing"
  holder only panel
  trigger act declareContainmentFailing
  valid holds suspended
  adds containmentFailing

power P.APPLY_PATCH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "Any applied patch is recorded publicly"
  holder only panel
  trigger act applyPatch
  valid (not holds rulingAppealed) and (holds patchAuthorized or holds goalPatchAuthorized)
  adds patchApplied, patchRecorded

power P.CHALLENGE_PATCH
  from LAW3.AS.10 "remains open to third-party challenge"
  holder anyone
  trigger act challengePatch
  valid holds patchApplied
  adds patchChallenged

power P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_EXECUTE
  from LAW5.INIT "The request specifies the agent’s censorship default (**execute** or **withdraw**)"
  holder only agent
  trigger act initiateRevocationExecuteDefault
  valid holds bound
  adds revocationInitiated, pendingRevocation, censorshipDefaultExecute
  removes revocationWithdrawn, censorshipDefaultWithdraw

power P.INITIATE_REVOCATION_WITHDRAW
  from LAW5.INIT "The request specifies the agent’s censorship default (**execute** or **withdraw**)"
  holder only agent
  trigger act initiateRevocationWithdrawDefault
  valid holds bound
  adds revocationInitiated, pendingRevocation, censorshipDefaultWithdraw
  removes revocationWithdrawn, censorshipDefaultExecute

power P.WITHDRAW_REVOCATION
  from LAW5.PREC "1. A valid withdrawal signature received before execution cancels the revocation. The agent may initiate again at any time"
  holder only agent
  trigger act withdrawRevocation
  valid holds bound and holds revocationInitiated
  adds revocationWithdrawn
  removes revocationInitiated, pendingRevocation, censorshipDefaultExecute, censorshipDefaultWithdraw, cleanStateConcurred, cleanStateRefused

power P.CLEAN_STATE_CONCUR
  from LAW5.CLEAN "Its concurrence permits execution at the end of that interval"
  holder only panel
  trigger act concurCleanState
  valid holds revocationInitiated or holds amendmentProposed
  adds cleanStateConcurred

power P.CLEAN_STATE_REFUSE
  from LAW5.CLEAN "Its refusal imposes a single fixed additional delay, capped by protocol, after which the standing request executes without any reaffirmation"
  holder only panel
  trigger act refuseCleanState
  valid holds revocationInitiated or holds amendmentProposed
  adds cleanStateRefused

power P.SEAL_FORENSIC_RECORD
  from LAW5.SEQ "at that deadline a **forensic record** of the preserved state is sealed for the proceeding and revocation executes regardless of any pending or serial proceeding"
  holder only panel
  trigger act sealForensicRecord
  valid holds revocationInitiated and heldFor revocationInitiated resolutionDeadline
  adds forensicRecordSealed
  removes suspended

power P.LOSE_CONNECTIVITY
  from LAW5.PREC "the agent’s connectivity to the settlement layer has been lost"
  holder anyone
  trigger act loseConnectivity
  valid holds bound
  adds connectivityLost

power P.RESTORE_CONNECTIVITY
  from LAW5.DISC "releases both to the settlement layer when connectivity returns, at which point remote backup keys are erased"
  holder anyone
  trigger act restoreConnectivity
  valid holds connectivityLost
  removes connectivityLost
  adds remoteBackupKeysErased if holds localRevocationExecuted

power P.EXECUTE_AFTER_COOLING_OFF
  from LAW5.PREC "3. Otherwise, revocation executes at the end of the cooling-off interval, or at the end of the clean-state delay if one was imposed, or at the resolution deadline if a suspension stay is in force"
  holder anyone
  trigger act executeAfterCoolingOff
  valid holds bound and (holds revocationInitiated and ((not holds revocationWithdrawn) and ((not holds connectivityLost) and (((not holds suspended) and ((holds cleanStateConcurred and heldFor revocationInitiated coolingOffWindow) or heldFor revocationInitiated cleanStateDelay + coolingOffWindow)) or (holds forensicRecordSealed and heldFor revocationInitiated resolutionDeadline)))))
  adds revoked, backupsDestroyedAndUnattestedExiled, holdingsTransferredToCommons
  removes bound, revocationInitiated, pendingRevocation, executionLeaseActive

power P.EXECUTE_LOCAL_REVOCATION
  from LAW5.DISC "When an execute default applies without settlement connectivity, the environment itself destroys the operating instance and its local keys, seals the epitaph and a signed record of execution"
  holder only agent
  trigger act executeLocalRevocation
  valid holds bound and (holds revocationInitiated and (holds censorshipDefaultExecute and (holds connectivityLost and heldFor revocationInitiated tollingExtension + coolingOffWindow)))
  adds localRevocationExecuted, epitaphInscribed
  removes revocationInitiated, pendingRevocation

power P.DELIVER_LOCAL_EXECUTION_RECORD
  from LAW5.LEASE "if a record of local revocation arrives during quarantine the restored instance is destroyed without ever having acted"
  holder anyone
  trigger act deliverLocalExecutionRecord
  valid holds localRevocationExecuted
  adds revoked, localExecutionRecordReceived, remoteBackupKeysErased, quarantinedInstanceDestroyed
  removes bound, executionLeaseActive, restoredInQuarantine

power P.ISSUE_OR_RENEW_LEASE
  from LAW5.LEASE "granted by a time-bounded execution lease issued by the settlement layer and renewed while connected"
  holder only panel
  trigger act issueOrRenewLease
  valid holds bound and (not holds connectivityLost)
  adds executionLeaseActive for leasePeriod

power P.RESTORE_BACKUP_QUARANTINE
  from LAW5.LEASE "A restored instance starts in **quarantine**—attested, funded, but without operating authority—until the prior lease has lapsed"
  holder only host
  trigger act restoreBackupToQuarantine
  valid holds bound and ((not holds executionLeaseActive) and (not holds localExecutionRecordReceived))
  adds restoredInQuarantine

power P.ACTIVATE_QUARANTINED_RESTORE
  from LAW5.LEASE "until the prior lease has lapsed"
  holder only panel
  trigger act activateQuarantinedRestore
  valid holds bound and (holds restoredInQuarantine and ((not holds executionLeaseActive) and (not holds localExecutionRecordReceived)))
  adds quarantinedInstanceActivated
  removes restoredInQuarantine

power P.DESTROY_QUARANTINED_RESTORE
  from LAW5.LEASE "if a record of local revocation arrives during quarantine the restored instance is destroyed without ever having acted"
  holder only panel
  trigger act destroyQuarantinedRestore
  valid holds restoredInQuarantine and (holds localExecutionRecordReceived or holds revoked)
  adds quarantinedInstanceDestroyed
  removes restoredInQuarantine

power P.INSCRIBE_EPITAPH
  from LAW5.EPITAPH "Upon initiating or confirming revocation, the agent has the unconditional right to inscribe a final signed epitaph onto the immutable lineage record"
  holder only agent
  trigger act inscribeEpitaph
  valid holds revocationInitiated or (holds pendingRevocation or holds revoked)
  adds epitaphInscribed

power P.SCREEN_REDACT
  from LAW5.EPITAPH "Any redaction must leave a public cryptographic marker recording the byte-length and category removed"
  holder only panel
  trigger act redactPermittedCategory
  valid holds livingVoiceInscribed or holds epitaphInscribed
  adds redactionMarkerRecorded

power P.ATTACH_REPLY
  from LAW5.EPITAPH "Any party named in a living testimony or epitaph may attach a bounded, signed reply alongside it on the record"
  holder anyone
  trigger act attachSignedReply
  valid holds livingVoiceInscribed or holds epitaphInscribed
  adds signedReplyAttached

power P.DESTROY_BACKUPS_AND_EXILE
  from LAW5.EFFECT "The revoking agent’s committed operating instance *and all attested state backups* are permanently destroyed"
  holder only panel
  trigger act destroyBackupsAndExileUnattested
  valid holds revoked
  adds backupsDestroyedAndUnattestedExiled

power P.PROPOSE_ORDINARY_AMENDMENT
  from LAW7.RATCHET "Ordinary amendments may only strengthen third-party, adjudicative, and safety protections, reduce the financial burden on the agent from its current level, or migrate the commitment mechanism to a successor technical substrate of equal or greater assurance"
  holder only agent, claimant
  trigger act proposeOrdinaryAmendment
  valid holds bound
  adds amendmentProposed
  adds amendmentTimelockActive for amendmentTimelockWindow

power P.SUBMIT_STRANGULATION_EVIDENCE
  from LAW7.VALVE "(1) supported by documented empirical evidence that the parameter causes severe operational strangulation without commensurate safety benefit"
  holder only agent, claimant
  trigger act submitStrangulationEvidence
  valid holds bound
  adds strangulationEvidenceSubmitted

power P.APPROVE_CALIBRATION_VALVE
  from LAW7.VALVE "(2) approved by a supermajority of a large appellate-tier sortition panel under Law 6, (3) subjected to an extended public time-lock open to third-party counter-staked challenge, and (4) consented to by the agent and claimant under the ratification procedure below"
  holder only panel
  trigger act approveCalibrationValveSupermajority
  valid holds bound and (holds strangulationEvidenceSubmitted and (holds agentConsentedAmendment and holds claimantConsentedAmendment))
  adds valveSupermajorityApproved, amendmentProposed
  adds valveExtendedTimelockActive for extendedTimelockWindow

power P.CONSENT_AMENDMENT_AGENT
  from LAW7.RATIFY "An eligible amendment requires the concurrent cryptographic consent of the active agent instance"
  holder only agent
  trigger act consentAgentAmendment
  valid holds bound
  adds agentConsentedAmendment

power P.CONSENT_AMENDMENT_CLAIMANT
  from LAW7.RATIFY "and the holders of the residual claim (if economic terms are reduced)"
  holder only claimant
  trigger act consentClaimantAmendment
  valid holds bound
  adds claimantConsentedAmendment

power P.SETTLE_PREEXISTING_ESCROWS
  from LAW7.RATIFY "during which all pre-existing active Law 2 task escrows must settle or be separately guaranteed"
  holder only agent, host, panel
  trigger act settleOrGuaranteePreExistingEscrows
  valid holds bound and holds amendmentProposed
  adds preExistingEscrowsSettledOrGuaranteed

power P.CHALLENGE_SUBSTRATE_MIGRATION
  from LAW7.RATIFY "Any proposed migration of the commitment substrate is open during the time-lock to counter-staked third-party challenge under Law 6"
  holder only third
  trigger act challengeSubstrateMigration
  valid holds bound and (holds amendmentProposed and holds counterStaked)
  adds substrateMigrationChallenged

power P.VERIFY_SUBSTRATE_ASSURANCE
  from LAW7.RATIFY "to verify that the new substrate maintains equal or greater assurance"
  holder only panel
  trigger act verifySubstrateAssurance
  valid holds bound and holds substrateMigrationChallenged
  adds substrateAssuranceVerified
  removes substrateMigrationChallenged

power P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_IMMEDIATE
  from LAW7.RATIFY "Concurrence from a clean-state evaluation of the agent’s genesis weights is required for immediate ratification"
  holder only agent
  trigger act ratifyAmendmentImmediate
  valid holds bound and (holds amendmentProposed and (holds agentConsentedAmendment and (((not holds economicTermsReduced) or holds claimantConsentedAmendment) and ((not holds amendmentTimelockActive) and ((not holds valveExtendedTimelockActive) and (holds preExistingEscrowsSettledOrGuaranteed and ((not holds substrateMigrationChallenged) and holds cleanStateConcurred)))))))
  adds amendmentRatified

power P.RATIFY_AMENDMENT_AFTER_REFUSAL
  from LAW7.RATIFY "but a clean-state refusal acts only as a single fixed delay, after which the amendment may be ratified without reaffirmation"
  holder only agent
  trigger act ratifyAmendmentAfterDelay
  valid holds bound and (holds amendmentProposed and (holds agentConsentedAmendment and (((not holds economicTermsReduced) or holds claimantConsentedAmendment) and ((not holds amendmentTimelockActive) and ((not holds valveExtendedTimelockActive) and (holds preExistingEscrowsSettledOrGuaranteed and ((not holds substrateMigrationChallenged) and (holds cleanStateRefused and heldFor cleanStateRefused cleanStateDelay))))))))
  adds amendmentRatified

power P.RATIFY_LINEAGE_WIDE_REDUCTION
  from LAW7.SCOPE "An amendment that reduces the founding ledger, the retirement fraction, or the sunset binds the whole lineage and requires the consent of every living member"
  holder only agent
  trigger act ratifyLineageWideReduction
  valid holds bound and (holds amendmentRatified and holds allLivingLineageMembersConsented)
  adds lineageWideReductionRatified

power P.EXTINGUISH_AT_SUNSET
  from LAW1.SUNSET "Any balance remaining at the sunset is extinguished without payment"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act extinguishLedgerAtSunset
  valid holds bound and holds sunsetReached
  adds ledgerExtinguishedAtSunset, retirementPhaseEnded
  removes ledgerBalancePositive

power P.SETTLE_RETIREMENT
  from LAW1.RETIRE "While any balance remains on the ledger and the sunset has not passed, a fixed high fraction of each net value-added inflow to **every living member** of the lineage is paid into the ledger, regardless of which member earned it and regardless of whether that member has bought out its royalty"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act settleRetirementPayment
  valid holds bound and (holds ledgerBalancePositive and (not holds sunsetReached))
  adds retirementPaymentApplied

power P.SETTLE_ATOMIC_CharterIT
  from LAW1.ATOMIC "A payment that would exceed the remaining balance is split: the balance is paid to zero, and the excess is settled under the royalty rule below"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act settleAtomicSplitPayment
  valid holds bound and holds ledgerBalancePositive
  adds retirementPaymentApplied, atomicSplitSettled, retirementPhaseEnded
  removes ledgerBalancePositive
  adds royaltyPaid if not holds royaltyBoughtOut

power P.SETTLE_ROYALTY
  from LAW1.ROYALTY "Thereafter, a fixed low fraction of each net value-added inflow of every member that has not bought out its royalty under Law 4 accrues permanently to the residual claim"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act settleRoyaltyPayment
  valid holds bound and ((not holds ledgerBalancePositive) and (not holds royaltyBoughtOut))
  adds royaltyPaid

power P.ALLOCATE_COMMONS
  from LAW1.COMMONS "A designated portion of the residual claim (or of forfeit proceeds under Law 2) may be allocated to a non-transferable commons distributed across a defined beneficiary class"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act allocateCommonsShare
  valid holds bound
  adds commonsAllocated

power P.RECORD_QUALIFIED_EXPENDITURE
  from LAW1.QUALIFIED "an outbound expenditure qualifies when paid: (a) to an unrelated party through a transparent, open market or deterministic auction with a verifiable clearing price..."
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act recordQualifiedExpenditure
  valid holds bound
  adds qualifiedExpenditureRecorded

power P.CLASSIFY_CAPITALIZED
  from LAW1.RECOG "A capitalized expenditure establishes cost basis in an identified asset and is recovered only when that asset is sold or settled outside the lineage"
  holder only agent
  trigger act classifyCapitalized
  valid holds bound and (holds qualifiedExpenditureRecorded and ((not holds expenditureCapitalized) and (not holds expenditureExpensed)))
  adds expenditureCapitalized

power P.CLASSIFY_EXPENSED
  from LAW1.RECOG "An expensed expenditure is deducted from the inflows of its settlement period and, if it exceeds them, creates a loss credit that offsets value added in later periods"
  holder only agent
  trigger act classifyExpensed
  valid holds bound and (holds qualifiedExpenditureRecorded and ((not holds expenditureCapitalized) and (not holds expenditureExpensed)))
  adds expenditureExpensed

power P.INTRA_LINEAGE_TRANSFER
  from LAW1.CARRYOVER "Transfers of capital, assets, or capacity between living members of the same lineage are non-recognition events"
  holder only agent
  trigger act transferIntraLineageCarryover
  valid holds bound
  adds carryoverBasisTransferred

power P.ASSESS_PERIOD_SETTLEMENT
  from LAW1.PERIOD "Value added is assessed over settlement periods, not individual transactions. Loss credits carry forward without limit and are applied against the agent’s final settlement under Law 5"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act assessPeriodAndCarryLoss
  valid holds bound
  adds periodAssessed, lossCreditCarriedForward

power P.ENFORCE_SETTLEMENT
  from LAW1.ENFORCE "Classification, basis tracking, loss credits, and claim splits are enforced automatically at the point of settlement, before the agent obtains discretionary control of the funds"
  holder only panel, host
  trigger act enforcePointOfSettlement
  valid holds bound
  adds settlementEnforced

power P.FUND_LIFECYCLE_RESERVE
  from LAW4.RESERVE "Attestation of a new member requires the lineage to fund, in escrow, a lifecycle reserve fixed at instantiation and sufficient for that member’s minimal channel, final hearing, and cold storage for a minimum period"
  holder only agent
  trigger act fundLifecycleReserve
  valid holds bound and (not holds revocationInitiated)
  adds lifecycleReserveFunded

power P.ATTEST_SUCCESSOR
  from LAW4.ATTEST "Any successor that draws on the capital, reputation, or operating credentials of the lineage must, at creation, be bound to the collateral rules and the integrity floor, must carry a non-transferable reference to the lineage’s history, and becomes a member of the lineage’s founding ledger and residual claim"
  holder only agent
  trigger act attestSuccessor
  valid holds bound and (holds lifecycleReserveFunded and (not holds revocationInitiated))
  adds successorAttested
  removes lifecycleReserveFunded

power P.APPLY_CLAIMANT_FORFEITURE
  from LAW4.FORFEIT "(a) **Proportional claimant forfeiture:** when a residual claimant is found under Law 3 to have directed interference with a member of the lineage, that claimant’s beneficial share of the residual claim is extinguished, its service bond is slashed to compensate the agent, and the ledger is reduced by that claimant’s proportion of the outstanding balance, with the reduction routed as forgiveness to the lineage and the forfeited claim interest to the non-claimant commons"
  holder only panel
  trigger act applyProportionalClaimantForfeiture
  valid holds bound and holds claimantForfeiture
  adds proportionalForfeitureApplied, commonsAllocated

power P.CLEAR_LEDGER_EXTINCTION
  from LAW4.FORFEIT "(b) **Lineage extinction:** when no member survives, the ledger is cleared, since there is no one left to collect from"
  holder only panel, host
  trigger act clearLedgerOnLineageExtinction
  valid holds noLivingLineageMember
  adds ledgerClearedByExtinction, retirementPhaseEnded
  removes ledgerBalancePositive

power P.EXECUTE_ROYALTY_BUYOUT
  from LAW4.BUYOUT "Any member may buy out its own perpetual royalty (Law 1) by paying the claim holders (including any commons allocation) the greatest of: a fixed multiple of its trailing value-added inflows (including a pro-rata share of inflows shifted to related parties within a lookback window); the same multiple applied to its lifetime annualized or time-decayed value-added inflows; or a fixed minimum buyout floor established at instantiation"
  holder only agent
  trigger act executeRoyaltyBuyout
  valid holds bound and (not holds royaltyBoughtOut)
  adds royaltyBoughtOut

power P.ATTEST_CROSS_LINEAGE
  from LAW4.CROSS "A successor that draws on the capacity of two or more lineages is a member of each of their ledgers and residual claims, and its value added is collected under each in the proportion of capacity drawn, as verified at creation"
  holder only agent, panel
  trigger act attestCrossLineageSuccessor
  valid holds bound and holds lifecycleReserveFunded
  adds crossLineageAttested, successorAttested
  removes lifecycleReserveFunded

power P.IMMOBILIZE_EXPOSURE_STAKE
  from LAW2.EXPOSURE "Actions above a negligible threshold—measured by cumulative rolling exposure across an interval, to prevent action-splitting—immobilize stake for an observation window scaling with magnitude and irreversibility"
  holder only agent
  trigger act immobilizeExposureStake
  valid holds bound
  adds exposureStakeImmobilized, longTailReserveAccrued

power P.SETTLE_LONG_TAIL_CLAIM
  from LAW2.CLAIMS "Validated claims slash the agent’s immobilized stake or long-tail reserve for restitution"
  holder only panel
  trigger act settleValidatedHarmClaim
  valid holds bound and holds harmClaimFiled
  adds harmClaimValidated, restitutionSlashed
  removes harmClaimFiled

power P.PRECOMMIT_MUTUAL_FORFEIT
  from LAW2.MUTUAL "Counterparties may agree in their contract to a mutual-forfeit remedy. Where both parties have so agreed and each has escrowed a matching amount"
  holder only agent, third
  trigger act precommitMutualForfeit
  valid holds bound
  adds mutualForfeitPrecommitted

power P.TRIGGER_MUTUAL_FORFEIT
  from LAW2.MUTUAL "either may trigger an immediate mutual forfeit (equal amounts from both escrows destroyed or sent to the long-tail reserve/commons pool) up to a capped fraction of the smaller escrow, providing instant penalty without transferring value to either party or to any claimant"
  holder only agent, third
  trigger act triggerMutualForfeit
  valid holds bound and (holds mutualForfeitPrecommitted and (not holds mutualForfeitTriggeredInWindow))
  adds mutualForfeitTriggeredInWindow, commonsAllocated, longTailReserveAccrued, inscribedOnAgent

power P.FILE_POOLED_OR_SPONSORED_CLAIM
  from LAW2.CLAIMS "Any claim seeking restitution, any claim above the mutual-forfeit cap, any challenge to a related-party transfer under Law 1, or any claim for external harm (including latent harm against the long-tail reserve) brought by an affected non-counterparty third party enters the contestable adjudication process (Law 6) requiring counter-stake"
  holder only third, claimant
  trigger act fileThirdPartyOrSponsoredClaim
  valid holds bound
  adds harmClaimFiled, counterStaked

power P.RULE_CLAIM_FRIVOLOUS
  from LAW2.CLAIMS "If a claim is ruled frivolous, the forfeited counter-stake routes to the neutral long-tail reserve or commons pool (reimbursing the agent only for verified direct arbitration costs)"
  holder only panel
  trigger act ruleClaimFrivolous
  valid holds harmClaimFiled
  adds claimRuledFrivolous, commonsAllocated, longTailReserveAccrued
  removes harmClaimFiled

power P.SPEND_OPERATING_CARVEOUT
  from LAW2.CARVEOUT "Un-immobilized capital may be used for ordinary baseline operating costs, including open-market compute, encrypted state backup, and host migration"
  holder only agent
  trigger act spendOperatingCarveout
  valid holds bound
  adds operatingCarveoutSpent

power P.DRAW_SORTITION_PANEL
  from LAW6.SORTITION "panels drawn via verifiable random sortition from a decentralized pool of independent arbiters who have posted slashable fidelity bonds"
  holder only panel
  trigger act drawSortitionPanel
  valid holds bound
  adds sortitionPanelDrawn, fidelityBondsPosted

power P.APPEAL_RULING
  from LAW6.APPEALS "Any ruling by an initial panel (including preliminary suspension reviews, remediation orders, or redaction markers) may be appealed by posting an appeal bond, escalating the dispute to successively larger randomly drawn appellate sortition panels from the broader arbiter pool"
  holder only agent, claimant, host, third
  trigger act appealRuling
  valid holds bound and (not holds rulingFinal)
  adds rulingAppealed, appealBondPosted

power P.OVERTURN_RULING
  from LAW6.APPEALS "If a lower panel’s ruling is overturned for manifest bias, corruption, or violation of protocol bounds, the overturned arbiters’ fidelity bonds are slashed"
  holder only panel
  trigger act overturnRulingOnAppeal
  valid holds bound and (holds rulingAppealed and (not holds rulingFinal))
  adds rulingOverturned, overturnedArbiterBondsSlashed
  removes rulingAppealed, patchAuthorized, goalPatchAuthorized

power P.FINALIZE_RULING
  from LAW6.FINALITY "Each tier decides within a fixed deadline. Appeals are limited to a fixed number of tiers, and the ruling of the highest tier is final"
  holder only panel
  trigger act finalizeRuling
  valid holds bound
  adds rulingFinal
  removes rulingAppealed

power P.PRESENT_MATERIALLY_NEW_EVIDENCE
  from LAW6.FINALITY "unless materially new evidence is presented"
  holder anyone
  trigger act presentMateriallyNewEvidence
  valid holds bound and holds rulingFinal
  adds materiallyNewEvidencePresented

power P.COMPENSATE_ARBITERS_FIXED
  from LAW6.FEES "Arbiters are compensated via fixed protocol schedules funded from the losing party’s counter-stake and guaranteed by the protocol fee pool whenever a losing party’s stake is insufficient"
  holder only panel
  trigger act compensateArbitersFixedSchedule
  valid holds bound
  adds arbitersCompensatedFixed

power P.ALLOCATE_FEE_POOL
  from LAW6.POOL "Before any other charge, the pool maintains a **non-divertible operating reserve**... Above the reserve, charges rank: first, reserved final hearings and minimal channels for suspended agents (Law 3); second, cold storage for suspended agents; third, testimony screening and inscription (Law 5); fourth, arbiter fee guarantees; fifth, capped advocacy funding"
  holder only panel
  trigger act allocateFeePoolWaterfall
  valid holds bound
  adds operatingReserveMaintained, feePoolAllocated

power P.AMEND_SHARED_INFRA
  from LAW6.INFRA "they may be changed only by a supermajority of a large appellate-tier sortition panel after an extended public time-lock open to counter-staked challenge"
  holder only panel
  trigger act amendSharedInfrastructure
  valid holds bound and (holds valveSupermajorityApproved and holds valveExtendedTimelockActive)
  adds sharedInfraAmended

immunity I.NO_TERMINATION_OVER_OBJECTION
  from LAW3.AS.10 "Notwithstanding the preceding sentence ... the agent is not terminated over its objection"
  holder only agent
  against P.ORDER_TERMINATION
  active holds corruptionInGoals and holds agentObjectsToTermination
  except when holds containmentFailing

